window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["2e"]={"https://theconversation.com/eurovision-2027-is-canada-singing-its-way-into-the-european-union-295040":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"f5a3b621e4ca9405d1351ccd07a08a3d847b4bdda0afe4e1bccdad82bf61a540","read":"https://theconversation.com/eurovision-2027-is-canada-singing-its-way-into-the-european-union-295040","bytes":185836,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Eurovision 2027: Is Canada singing its way into the European Union?","by":[{"n":"Petra Dolata","r":"Associate Professor, History, University of Calgary"}],"pub":"2026-10-28T10:55:49Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Officials are meeting this week for the ",["21st Canada-European Union Leaders’ summit","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/10/25/prime-minister-carney-host-canada-european-union-summit-montreal"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It comes only a month after European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen ",["offered Canada associate membership","https://commission.europa.eu/strategy-and-policy/state-union_en"],". ",["A draft statement from Montréal","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/european-union-canada-associate-member-9.7399578"],", where Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney, von der Leyen and EU Council President António Costa met for two days to discuss strengthening ties, calls for an “ever closer association” that will result “in a more active foreign and security policy partnership.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The talks ",["follow a series","https://www.international.gc.ca/world-monde/international_relations-relations_internationales/eu-ue/agreement-accord.aspx?lang=eng"]," of ",["milestones","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/04/28/prime-minister-carney-represent-canada-first-time-european-political"]," in the relationship between the transatlantic partners, including the ",["announcement in July","https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/jul/01/canada-joins-eurovision-song-contest"]," that Canada was joining the Eurovision song contest. It’s the first country to do so since Australia entered in 2015."]},{"k":"p","s":["Eurovision is held every year in May, with member countries submitting one original song. Over the years, the event’s format has changed from an exclusive jury vote to a viewer televote and today’s combination of both."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sometimes, voting ",["can become political","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/eurovision-canada-politics-soft-power-1.6841812"],", with viewers voting according to their ",["geopolitical preferences","https://www.chathamhouse.org/publications/the-world-today/2023-04/eurovision-war-and-geopolitics-pop"]," or diaspora communities casting ballots for their former home countries regardless of the quality of the performance."]},{"k":"p","s":["This may be good news for Canada, which is currently basking in European affection. The current ",["geopolitical romance","https://www.policymagazine.ca/the-canada-eu-romance-friends-with-benefits-or-cautionary-fairy-tale/"]," between Canada and the EU could help a Canadian song win. It wouldn’t be the first Canadian win, though. ",["Céline Dion took home the prize in 1988","https://ici.radio-canada.ca/rci/en/news/2165332/celine-dion-cheers-on-eurovision-contest-as-fans-hope-for-surprise-performance-at-final"],", representing Switzerland."]},{"k":"h","s":["Uranium fears in the 1950s"]},{"k":"p","s":["The EU and Canada are clearly getting closer. But will historians look back at Eurovision and other developments as the beginning of comprehensive Canada-EU integration? Probably not — and history shows why."]},{"k":"p","s":["A look at the history of Canada-EU relations reveals a shared interest in deeper integration that has rarely materialized into anything concrete."]},{"k":"p","s":["More than half a century ago, a couple of years after the 1957 ",["Treaty of Rome","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/about-parliament/en/in-the-past/the-parliament-and-the-treaties/treaty-of-rome"]," had established the ",["European Economic Community","https://www.econlib.org/library/Enc/EuropeanEconomicCommunity.html"]," and ",["the European Atomic Energy Community","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/about-parliament/en/in-the-past/the-parliament-and-the-treaties/euratom-treaty"],", Canada was the first industrialized country to sign an agreement with the latter organization. In October 1959, Canada became a signatory to the ",["Peaceful Uses of Atomic Energy","https://carleton.ca/ces/eulearning/economics/ceta/canada-and-the-eu-an-overview/"]," deal."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the time, Canada was worried about losing the United States as a major export market for its uranium. That’s because the U.S. had only agreed to a supply contract until 1962, expecting much lower demand for Canadian uranium after that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prime Minister John Diefenbaker, who wanted to diversify Canada’s trade relations and revive imperial links with the United Kingdom, ",["looked to Europe for future uranium markets","https://www.commonwealthroundtable.co.uk/commonwealth/americas/canada/canadian-concerns-of-a-different-kind-of-brexit-britains-first-application-to-the-eec-and-canadas-commonwealth-appeal/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["He added Germany and Italy to the list of countries to buy Canadian uranium. Canada also tried to ensure these new customers would only use the uranium for peaceful purposes."]},{"k":"p","s":["To do so, Canada considered an agreement with the European Atomic Energy Community, of which both West Germany and Italy were member states, as the best option. For its part, the organization believed the agreement with Canada not only provided access to Canadian uranium and civilian nuclear technology but also gave it international visibility."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in retrospect, beyond scientific collaboration, not much else was achieved. Canada had already lost the race to the U.S., whose aggressive export policy led to Western Europe adopting American nuclear technology."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nixon-Trudeau tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diversification away from the U.S. was also behind the ",["1976 framework agreement for commercial and economic co-operation","https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:21976A0706(01)&qid=1793021640385"],", which Canada signed as the first industrialized country with the ",["European Community","https://www.britannica.com/topic/European-Community-European-economic-association"],", which later became the European Union."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada was surprised by U.S. President ",["Richard Nixon’s 1971 announcement of a new economic program","https://doi.org/10.1111/ehr.13052"]," that abolished the conversion of gold to American dollars and terminated fixed exchange rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada hadn’t been warned about the immediate imposition of a unilateral 10 per cent surcharge on imports, and it wasn’t exempted. In response to these Nixon shocks and fuelled by long-simmering anxieties about Canadian independence, ",["the Liberal government under Pierre Trudeau proposed a third option","https://doi.org/10.1080/02722010409481207"]," to reduce dependence on the U.S. and actively seek new partnerships, mostly with Europe."]},{"k":"p","s":["As they did in the late 1950s, the Europeans were receptive to Canadian advances because they wanted ",["access to Canada’s energy resources","https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-43250-8_55"],". This was especially true in the wake of the 1973 oil crisis, which had not only caused Western European countries to desperately search for oil supplies outside the Middle East and the Soviet Union, but also led to ",["their heightened demands for uranium","https://doi.org/10.1080/07036338108428800"]," as nuclear power programs ramped up to provide alternative energy."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the framework agreement between Canada and European countries never realized its full potential. Instead, ",["Canada deepened its relations with the U.S. and signed a free-trade agreement in the 1980s","https://doi.org/10.3138/9781442689541"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Can momentum be sustained?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Today, Canada faces another trade crisis with the U.S. Canadian oil and gas is in high demand, even in a decarbonizing Europe that’s cut off from Russian supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, the ",["current nuclear renaissance","https://www.cbc.ca/radio/frontburner/carney-nuclear-renaissance-9.7296011"],", the combined result of climate change action and fossil fuel geopolitics, has made Canada’s uranium a highly sought-after resource."]},{"k":"p","s":["No wonder the EU and Canada are seemingly moving closer. But will the rhetoric around ",["middle power solidarity","https://theconversation.com/mark-carneys-davos-speech-marks-a-major-departure-from-canadas-usual-approach-to-the-u-s-274090"]," and common values be enough to sustain the momentum?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Europeans and Canadians have always seen each other as friends, and Canada’s Eurovision participation will only cement that war relationship. But historically, closer ties have not led to deeper integration in the long run."]}],"chars":5602},"https://theconversation.com/friday-essay-to-tackle-the-dreadful-rise-in-antisemitism-we-must-speak-the-truth-about-israels-war-crimes-296263":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"ac8e29a747e97f91072af8cc5669acda8ea544a148050af03aacad7607794230","read":"https://theconversation.com/friday-essay-to-tackle-the-dreadful-rise-in-antisemitism-we-must-speak-the-truth-about-israels-war-crimes-296263","bytes":208563,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Friday essay: to tackle the dreadful rise in antisemitism, we must speak the truth about Israel’s war crimes","by":[{"n":"Robert Manne","r":"Emeritus Professor of Politics, La Trobe University"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T19:03:45Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Over the past weeks I have watched with interest the ways, following the horrific Hamas-led massacre of 1,200 Israelis on ",["October 7 2023","https://theconversation.com/three-years-after-october-7-global-attention-on-gaza-has-receded-the-real-test-will-come-after-israels-election-292360"],", prominent Jews with a connection to Australia have justified, in response, the killing by the Israel Defence Forces, or IDF, of around 75,000 Gazan Palestinians, the majority of whom were innocent civilians, or ",["more than 20,000","https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/06/1167790"]," babies or children."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recently, the British historian, Lord ",["Andrew Roberts","https://www.andrew-roberts.net/"],", was interviewed by Geraldine Doogue on the ABC Radio National program ",["Global Roaming","https://www.abc.net.au/listen/programs/global-roaming/lord-andrew-roberts-on-bondi-oct-7/107109506"],". According to Lord Roberts, the massacre of the Israeli Jews by Hamas and ",["Islamic Jihad","https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/sanctions/1267/aq_sanctions_list/summaries/entity/islamic-jihad-group"]," was an unspeakable moral crime, while the killing by the IDF of perhaps 40 or 50 times as many innocent Palestinians, was the kind of thing that, alas, happens in fighting a just war."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even the propaganda department of the IDF has barely challenged the estimates of the numbers of civilian deaths. However, without pointing to any evidence, Roberts claimed the number of innocent Palestinians massacred by the IDF had been greatly exaggerated."]},{"k":"p","s":["What was more interesting, however, was Roberts’ contrast between the killing of the Jews and Palestinians since the massacre of October 7. According to Roberts, the October 7 Hamas killers were in a “frenzy”. The things they did were “foul”, “vicious” and “disgusting”, resembling the accounts of warfare during “medieval” times and in recent history of the Japanese at “the ",["rape of Nanking","https://www.britannica.com/event/Nanjing-Massacre"],"”. With “civilised countries”, this kind of “frenzied killing” did not take place."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Gaza, the IDF’s killings were “totally different you see”. He said:"]},{"k":"p","s":["At no point did the Israelis look into the eyes of Palestinians and murder their children after torturing and raping them […] It’s an entirely different kind of warfare. You get tanks of course and aeroplanes […] Also of course you’ve got to kill as many terrorists as possible […] They [Hamas] also don’t care how many of their population die. In fact, in terms of public relations the more that die the better […] As an historian I try to stay rational and logical […] I see a totally different thing between the face-to-face massacre after torture and rape of Israelis on the 7th of October and the warfare that took place in Gaza between the IDF and Hamas."]},{"k":"p","s":["The IDF’s post-October 7 destruction in Gaza involved anything but conventional warfare. Anyone who has followed the Israeli campaign knows the Palestinians were killed according to an AI program called “Lavender”. It was first revealed in an article in ",["the 972 Magazine","https://www.972mag.com/lavender-ai-israeli-army-gaza/"]," on April 3 2024, written by Yuval Abraham, one of the filmmakers of the documentary ",["NAZA","https://theconversation.com/naza-harrowing-documentary-shows-how-killing-in-gaza-became-just-another-days-work-293710"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["When NAZA was shown at the Venice Film Festival, ",["the applause lasted","https://www.youtube.com/shorts/D-mnu76-tEQ"]," for 24 minutes. Israel had complete control of the air. The number of Palestinians who could be taken out as “collateral damage” – 20, 50, even 100 – depended on the seniority of the member of Hamas the IDF intelligence believed was sleeping in the same building."]},{"k":"p","s":["If Roberts had thought for five minutes about his black-and-white contrast between the Hamas killing of Israelis and the IDF killings of Palestinians in the most recent war in Gaza, it might have occurred to him that in the Holocaust, which Roberts almost certainly would regard as the darkest crime in the history of humankind, the Germans did not kill most of the six million Jews in a “frenzy” or in “face-to-face” combat\"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Eventually, the SS leadership recognised the most efficient and orderly method of exterminating the Jews was with deception. Vast numbers of the Jews who were murdered in the Holocaust were led naked into the gas chambers of the extermination camps, believing they were about to be showered. (Or in the case of my maternal grandfather, into a sealed truck in ",["Chelmno","https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/chelmno"],".)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Does Roberts believe this was a more civilised way of killing Jews than, for example, the often frenzied face-to-face pogroms that broke out during the ",["Russian Civil War","https://www.britannica.com/event/Russian-Civil-War"],", where tens of thousands of Jews were murdered?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Any judgement about the comparative morality of Hamas’ frenzied, hate-filled killing of Jews on October 7 and Israel’s nonchalant, formulaic, algorithmic killing of innocent Palestinians in response, is to my mind dauntingly difficult. Not so, apparently, for Lord Roberts."]},{"k":"h","s":["‘Jew hatred’ and genocide"]},{"k":"p","s":["In late October, Schwartz Media, owned by Morry Schwartz, published a Jewish Quarterly essay (edited by Jonathan Pearlman), ",["Jew-Hatred: The Latest Episode","https://jewishquarterly.com/essay/2026/10/jew-hatred"],", by the distinguished British historian, Sir Simon Schama. One of Schama’s contentions is that the claim the IDF has committed genocide against the Palestinians is “the most consequential” contemporary expression of millennia-old Jew-hatred."]},{"k":"p","s":["Almost everything Schama says about the crime of genocide is false."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to Schama, genocide is “the organised, systematic extermination of an entire population; a ",["Wannsee","https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/wannsee-conference-and-the-final-solution"]," -type, planned mass murder”. Schama seems not to recognise that largely because of the passionate political struggle of ",["Raphael Lemkin","https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/coining-a-word-and-championing-a-cause-the-story-of-raphael-lemkin"],", in 1948, genocide became a crime under international law."]},{"k":"p","s":["When an international court will decide whether or not Israel is guilty of genocide against the Palestinians in Gaza, it will do so not according to Schama’s Holocaust-inflected private definition, but according to law – the ",["Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide","https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/convention-prevention-and-punishment-crime-genocide"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Convention outlines what the International Commission of Jurists describes as “five specific underlying acts, any one of which may be constitutive of the crime of genocide”."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are: “killing members of a national, ethnical, racial or religious group”; “causing serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group”; “deliberately inflicting on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part; \"imposing measures to prevent births within the group”; or “forcibly transferring children of the group to another group”."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the genocide case is heard before an international court, one of the most important questions will be Israel’s intent. Here is all Schama says on this vital question about Israel’s arguably genocidal post October 7 massacres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Did Israel’s Minister of Defense, Yoav Gallant, not call Palestinians “human animals” and wish out loud for their extermination?"]},{"k":"p","s":["No, he did not. On 9 October 2023, as details of unspeakable atrocities were becoming known, Gallant used the phrase when speaking of the Hamas terrorists who had planned and executed the horrific massacre, whose power — and if necessary whose lives — he wished to see ended. Therein lies the difference between war and genocide."]},{"k":"p","s":["What ",["Gallant actually said","https://www.icj.org/resource-region/middle-east-and-north-africa/palestine/"]," was quite different:"]},{"k":"p","s":["I have ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel, everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we act accordingly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under conditions of total siege, the principal victims will, of course, be the civilian population of Gaza. Without food and water, everyone suffers, eventually everyone dies. The Gazan Palestinians, not just the Hamas terrorists, are Gallant’s “human animals”. One day later, to underline the point, Gallant promised: “Gaza won’t return to what it was before. We will eliminate everything.” Not Hamas; everything."]},{"k":"p","s":["More importantly, as all those who write about the events in Gaza should know, when South Africa ",["outlined its case","https://www.icj-cij.org/sites/default/files/case-related/192/192-20231228-app-01-00-en.pdf"]," to the International Court of Justice about Israel’s commission of genocide, it devoted nine tight, carefully footnoted pages to the question of Israel’s genocidal intent regarding the Palestinians in Gaza. What follows is a small sample."]},{"k":"p","s":["Time and again, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu described the coming battle between the Jews and the Palestinians as a war between light and darkness, civilisation and barbarism, good and evil. As Israel prepared for its ground invasion, Netanyahu called upon Israeli troops to “remember Amalek”. In the Torah, as the invasion of Amalek territory begins, the Jews are commanded by God: “Spare no one, but kill alike men and women, infants and sucklings.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On October 12, the president of Israel, Isaac Herzog, made clear that “the entire nation” of the Gazan Palestinians was responsible for what occurred on October 7. And that the nation’s “backbone” must be “broken” as a result."]},{"k":"p","s":["Three days earlier, the Coordinator of Government Activity in the Territories, Major General Ghassan Alian, had warned: “Human animals are dealt with accordingly. Israel has imposed a total blockade on Gaza, no electricity, no water […] You wanted hell, you will get hell.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On October 11, Ezra Yachin, a 95-year-old veteran of the notorious and brutal 1948 massacre of Palestinians at ",["Deir Yassin","https://www.britannica.com/place/Deir-Yassin"],", was wheeled out. He broadcast on social media: “Erase the memory of them [the Gazan Palestinians]. Erase them, their families, mothers and children. These animals can no longer live.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On October 13, the Minister for Energy and Infrastructure, Israel Katz, tweeted: “All the civilian population in Gaza […] will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On November 1, the Minister for Heritage, Amichai Eliyahu, described the north of Gaza as “more beautiful than ever. Everything is blown up and flattened, simply a pleasure for the eyes.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On November 11, the Minister for Agriculture, Avi Dichter, described what was happening as “the Gaza Nakba”. ",["Nakba","https://theconversation.com/the-nakba-75-years-after-losing-their-home-the-palestinians-are-still-experiencing-the-catastrophe-205413"],", the catastrophe, is the Palestinian name for the killings and the expulsions of 700,000 Palestinians at the time of the Arab–Jewish War of 1948."]},{"k":"p","s":["On December 25, a former ",["Knesset","https://www.britannica.com/topic/Knesset"]," member was reported thus: “I tell you, in Gaza without exception, they are all terrorists, sons of dogs. They must be exterminated, all of them killed.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["I hope not to be misunderstood. I have no idea whether the evidence collected by the South Africans or by others will eventually convince an international court of Israel’s commission of genocide in Gaza. I do know, however, that Schama’s suggestion that the “human animals” remark of Yoav Gallant was restricted to Hamas terrorists and did not involve the entire Palestinian population in Gaza, and that it was the sole or principal piece of evidence of Israeli post October 7 genocidal intent, are both false."]},{"k":"p","s":["Towards the end of his essay, Schama writes:"]},{"k":"p","s":["So, for all the chants, this paroxysm of rage is, at its psychological core, not about Palestine, Israel or even the Jews. The hatred is about the haters: a failure of self-recognition: a displacement of the obligation to make amends. The Nazification of Israel […] act[s] as a reprieve from failing to do much about saving the Jewish victims even after the facts of their annihilation [in the Holocaust] were known. Likewise framing the Jews as history’s paradigmatic imperialist oppressors spares the descendants of actual colonisers from too much critical self-examination. Put the Jews in the dock rather than your great-grandparents."]},{"k":"p","s":["I do not know how much Schama knows about Australia. However, the idea that the group Schama calls “white progressives”, including Australians, are trying to hide the guilt they ought to feel about the Indigenous dispossession in Australia, by defaming Israel for its supposedly genocidal campaign in Gaza, is about as comprehensive a misunderstanding of the politics of Gaza in this country as it is possible to imagine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Schama argues, repeatedly, that those who accuse Israel of genocide in Gaza know nothing of the Holocaust. I am not sure how he can also, absurdly and contradicting himself, claim the genocide accusers are displacing onto Israel the guilt they ought to feel about their country’s failure to save the Jews during the Holocaust, of whose history they are supposedly ignorant."]},{"k":"p","s":["More importantly, the hundreds of thousands of Australians who have demonstrated for the Gazan Palestinians – for the murdered, the wounded, the surviving two million whose lives lie in ruins – are overwhelmingly the same people who lead the struggle in Australia for Indigenous rights and the recognition of the tragedy of Indigenous dispossession."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the very head of those who march and chant for the Palestinians against what they believe to be Israel’s genocide in Gaza are Australia’s younger Indigenous leaders."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the conclusion of his denigration of the people who have reacted with appropriate horror at Israel’s pitiless destruction of Gaza, Schama thinks he can still speak with kindness, even intimacy, to the Palestinian people. “[S]hould we, Jews and non-Jews, Israelis and Palestinians, fail to listen to each other with respectful attention, informed by the truth, the unhappy victims of such deafness will, in the end, be all of us.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["A better title for Jew-Hatred would be Chutzpah."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jillian Segal’s ‘astonishing overreach’"]},{"k":"p","s":["In October, Jillian Segal AO, Australia’s special envoy to combat antisemitism, published ",["her progress report","https://www.aseca.gov.au/sites/default/files/2026-10/combatting-antisemitism-special-envoys-priorities.pdf"]," into the curse of rising antisemitism in Australia. The content has been expertly summarised ",["in Deepcut News","https://www.deepcutnews.com/p/its-time-to-sack-jillian-segal-jeff"]," by Jeffrey Loewenstein, a former chairman of the Anti-Defamation Commission in Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["“If Segal has her way, nearly every facet of life in Australia would, in effect, be subject to vetting by a cohort of pro-Israel supporters who wish for us to be muzzled as Israel carries out the worst crimes imaginable,” he wrote."]},{"k":"p","s":["“The unelected Segal wants to reshape the arts, vet our public broadcasters, oversee the use of venues, stages, art spaces, what festivals should and should not be doing, revise our visa programs, sit atop digital governance and online regulation and tell universities how to conduct themselves. The gall of the overreach is extraordinary and yet mainstream media freely aired Segal’s report and arguments with barely a care for its implications on Australian democracy.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beyond this astonishing overreach, what emerges from Segal is an even more alarming dimension of her progress report."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 14 occasions, Segal recommends the adoption throughout Australian institutions of the International Holocaust Remembrance Alliance’s ",["definition of antisemitism","https://holocaustremembrance.com/resources/working-definition-antisemitism"],". The reason seems clear. Despite acknowledging not every criticism of Israel or its government is antisemitic, time and again the IHRA definition links criticism of Israel and antisemitism."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to IHRA, it is antisemitic to claim that Israel exaggerates the Holocaust. It is antisemitic to accuse Jews of being more loyal to Israel than to their own homelands. It is antisemitic to deny Jews their right to self-determination or to describe Israel “as a racist endeavour”. It is antisemitic to compare Israel’s policies to those of the Nazis. And it is antisemitic to hold Jews in the diaspora responsible for Israel’s actions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the IHRA definition, everyone in Australia who criticises Israel’s policies in Gaza and the West Bank, or the diaspora for its uncritical support of those policies, will have to be very careful they have not strayed into territory the IHRA definition has forbidden and become vulnerable to the charge of antisemitism."]},{"k":"p","s":["An addition to the Segal agenda in her recent progress report is the claim the most important camp of antisemitism in Australia is to be found among left-wing progressives:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Modern, progressive antisemitism is the most pervasive manifestation of antisemitism facing Australia today […] Modern progressive antisemitism has grown out of, and is especially prevalent in, some institutions of intellectual and cultural leadership, including universities, media, arts organisations and human rights NGOs […] The claims that Israel has committed humanity’s worst crimes — including genocide, ethnic cleansing and apartheid — allow for the depiction of anyone who associates or aligns with Israel as complicit in its purported evil."]},{"k":"p","s":["As it happens, Segal has supplied us, by implication, with plentiful examples of what she takes to be modern, progressive antisemitism in Australia and elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to Segal, anyone who claims Israel has committed genocide in Gaza, as do very many international human rights bodies and genocide scholars, is an antisemite. According to Segal, anyone who believes it is almost self-evident that by destroying the houses, hospitals, schools, universities, mosques, cultural sites, agricultural lands, etc., Israel has been conducting a ruthless policy of ethnic cleansing in Gaza, thwarted only by the failure of Israel to find a country willing to take the two million survivors, is an antisemite."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to Segal, anyone who argues that by turning a blind eye to the daily attacks on the Palestinian villagers by the Jewish settlers, Israel has begun upon a policy of ethnic cleansing in the West Bank, is an antisemite. And according to Segal, anyone who argues the combination of liberal and democratic rights for the citizens of Israel and the suppression of those rights for the Palestinians in the West Bank (and now also most of Gaza) resembles the former system of apartheid in South Africa, is an antisemite."]},{"k":"p","s":["By labelling as antisemitism the opinions of a goodly part of the Australian left, and beyond that the politically informed public, the Segal report represents the most insidious attack on political free speech in the recent history of Australia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Asking to be left alone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Throughout my life, I have been preoccupied by the evil of antisemitism. One of my books, ",["The Culture of Forgetting: Helen Demidenko and the Holocaust","https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/14060105-the-culture-of-forgetting"],", was about Helen “Demidenko’s” celebrated novel, ",["The Hand that Signed the Paper","https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/36258559-the-hand-that-signed-the-paper"],". The novel revived the key Nazi concept that drove the Holocaust: Bolshevism and Stalinism as the expression of Jewish political power."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another of my books, ",["The Mind of the Islamic State","https://www.blackincbooks.com.au/news/discussing-dangerous-ideas-robert-manne"],", analysed the vicious antisemitism of ISIS. Accordingly, there is one eloquent passage in Schama with which I wholeheartedly agree:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Honestly, all we are asking for is to be left alone, to be able to send our children and grandchildren to a Jewish school in their uniforms, maybe with a kippah on their heads, without their being screamed at and being made to feel frightened and ashamed; to be able to ride public transport without being spat at or assaulted; to go to synagogue without having to pass through protective men with guns …"]},{"k":"p","s":["Schama believes he can help combat the rise of antisemitism in the diaspora by defending the indefensible: the war crimes of the IDF under Benjamin Netanyahu."]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe a more likely remedy would be for leading diaspora thinkers, like Schama, and influential publishers, like Morry Schwartz, and the leaders in Australia of the principal Israel and Jewish lobbies, like Jillian Segal, to speak the truth about what, under Netanyahu and the two ",["Kahanist","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Meir-Kahane"]," -fascist members of his Government, Israel has become."]},{"k":"p","s":["And about the moral revolution that has to happen in Israel if Jews in the diaspora are to be spared from the dreadful rise of antisemitism that is spreading around the Western world."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is an edited version of ",["an article originally published","https://robertmanne.substack.com/p/on-the-rise-of-antisemitism-in-australia"]," on Robert Manne’s Substack."]}],"chars":18886},"https://theconversation.com/how-north-korea-became-a-world-leader-in-state-sponsored-hacking-295597":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"27327d40d98cb12d8f25bd117b7c2724a0d6901629125b878a7c1fa2ea29a83f","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-north-korea-became-a-world-leader-in-state-sponsored-hacking-295597","bytes":183628,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How North Korea became a world leader in state-sponsored hacking","by":[{"n":"Jinkyung Baek","r":"PhD Candidate in Politics Research, King's College London"}],"pub":"2026-11-03T08:52:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Binance, the world’s largest cryptocurrency exchange, was the victim of a massive heist in late October. Approximately US$6.36 billion (£4.74 billion) of funds were stolen within the space of 20 minutes in an attack that has been described as the largest of its kind in history."]},{"k":"p","s":["The source of the ",["attack","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cqrmynd3042gt"]," has not yet been officially confirmed. But the ",["FBI","https://www.fbi.gov/investigate/cyber/alerts/2026/north-korea-responsible-for-6-billion-binance-attack"]," and blockchain analytics company ",["TRM Labs","https://www.trmlabs.com/resources/blog/north-korea-steals-usd-6-36-billion-from-binance-in-the-largest-hack-in-history"]," identified North Korea’s TraderTraitor hacking unit as the group most likely to have been behind it. Two other blockchain analytics firms, ",["Chainalysis","https://www.chainalysis.com/blog/binance-exploit-latest-findings-and-response/"]," and ",["Elliptic","https://www.elliptic.co/insights/binance-largest-hack-in-history/"],", have supported this attribution."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not the first time ",["North Korea","https://theconversation.com/topics/north-korea-2060"]," has been linked to cyber-attacks. Several other cryptocurrency exchange thefts in recent years have been attributed to North Korean state-sponsored hackers. These include the ",["2019 Upbit","https://world.kbs.co.kr/service/news_view.htm?lang=e&Seq_Code=189232"]," and ",["2025 Bybit","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c2kgndwwd7lo"]," hacks, where funds worth US$42 million and US$1.5 billion respectively were stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Therefore, while Pyongyang has always denied any involvement in state-sponsored cyber warfare, it is not surprising that North Korea has once again been mentioned in connection with a major crypto heist."]},{"k":"h","s":["State-sponsored hacking"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea’s cyber operations are the product of decades of strategic development. The North Korean state began ",["building","https://www.38north.org/wp-content/uploads/pdf/2020-0228_SKA_NK-Cyber-Operations.pdf"]," the technological foundations for these operations in the 1980s, establishing ",["domestic computing infrastructure","https://www.38north.org/wp-content/uploads/pdf/2020-0228_SKA_NK-Cyber-Operations.pdf"],", ",["specialised educational institutions","https://web.archive.org/web/20040418233326/http:/www.nis.go.kr/eng/north/education20.html"]," and state-led research centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["The development of its cyber capabilities ",["intensified","https://publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm201719/cmselect/cmdfence/327/32707.htm"]," in the 1990s. The ",["Korea Computer Center","https://thediplomat.com/2022/07/mapping-major-milestones-in-the-evolution-of-north-koreas-cyber-program/"]," was set up in 1990 to oversee national IT development. And in 1995, North Korea’s then-leader, Kim Jong-il, ",["directed the military","https://www.38north.org/wp-content/uploads/pdf/2020-0228_SKA_NK-Cyber-Operations.pdf"]," to develop cyber capabilities as a strategic component of national defence."]},{"k":"p","s":["IT education was further institutionalised from 1998 onward after computer education was made compulsory for all students from the fourth year of middle school."]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea began conducting major cyber-attacks in the 2000s. Early operations primarily targeted South Korea. But its cyber operations gradually expanded beyond the Korean peninsula, with the ",["2017 WannaCry attack","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-39919249"]," a prominent example of this development."]},{"k":"p","s":["This attack targeted computers running the Microsoft Windows operating system and ",["demanded ransom payments","https://techcrunch.com/2019/05/12/wannacry-two-years-on/"]," in the form of bitcoin cryptocurrency. It was ",["estimated to have","https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2017/12/19/571854614/u-s-says-north-korea-directly-responsible-for-wannacry-ransomware-attack"]," affected more than 300,000 computers across 150 countries, causing ",["billions","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-us-canada-42407488"]," of US dollars in damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea’s state-led cyber operations start with the ",["selection of young students","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2011/6/20/north-korea-recruits-hackers-at-school"]," who demonstrate outstanding academic performance, particularly in science and mathematics. These students are provided with specialised computer training at the elite Kumsong Middle School in Pyongyang."]},{"k":"p","s":["They then advance to one of ",["several colleges","https://www.chosun.com/english/national-en/2013/04/08/FQOCNI553NJT2I43EZDIKEI3TQ/"],", including Mirim College, Moranbong College, ",["Kim Il Sung University","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2011/6/20/north-korea-recruits-hackers-at-school"]," or the Kim Chaek University of Technology. In these colleges, students ",["undergo training programmes","https://www.hrnk.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/RGB_Final.pdf"]," combining military studies with advanced cyber skills."]},{"k":"p","s":["As of 2024, North Korea was ",["estimated to have","https://www.donga.com/en/article/all/20240731/5091529/1"]," trained roughly 8,400 state-sponsored cyber personnel through these programmes. This figure is likely to have increased since then."]},{"k":"h","s":["Clear strategic goals"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Korea’s investment in cyber personnel training is driven by clear strategic goals. The main objectives of early North Korean cyber-attacks were to create social disruption in what Pyongyang sees as hostile states."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples include the ",["2013 DarkSeoul attack","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-asia-23042334"]," and the 2014 cyber-attack on ",["Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power","https://www.piie.com/blogs/north-korea-witness-transformation/more-cyber-korea-hydro-and-nuclear-power-company-khnp"],". In the DarkSeoul attack, around 32,000 computers belonging to major South Korean broadcasting networks and financial institutions were disrupted by malware."]},{"k":"p","s":["The attack on Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power involved the theft and disclosure of personal employee information, nuclear power plant blueprints and technical documents. Both attacks aimed to disrupt critical systems and generate public anxiety. They allowed North Korea to exert pressure on its adversaries without engaging in direct military confrontation."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent years, however, North Korea’s cyber operations have shifted towards making money. The more recent cyber operations are part of the country’s broader efforts to ",["maintain regime stability","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5yn8eqg3npo"]," and fund its nuclear programme following years of international sanctions."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, a UN panel of experts ",["estimated","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/how-crypto-hacking-funds-isolated-north-korea-nuclear-programme"]," that the money stolen in North Korean cyber-attacks generated half of North Korea’s foreign currency income. One unnamed panel member added that stolen money funds “40% of the weapons of mass destruction programmes”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Several measures are in place to defend against North Korean cyber operations. These include financial sanctions and international efforts to disrupt money-laundering networks. Governments worldwide also ",["work closely with","https://www.secretservice.gov/newsroom/releases/2026/04/operation-atlantic-disrupts-more-45-million-cryptocurrency-fraud-freezes"]," the private sector to exchange intelligence, identify suspicious transactions and trace and recover stolen cryptocurrency."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the current measures have not been sufficient to prevent attacks. A key reason for this is the fact that international investigations and enforcement remain constrained by ",["national jurisdictions and sovereignty","https://sherloc.unodc.org/cld/pt/education/tertiary/cybercrime/module-7/key-issues/sovereignty-and-jurisdiction.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As in the physical world, one country cannot access data or conduct an investigation within another country’s territory without its consent. Digital evidence can be also be quickly deleted or altered, so reliance on international cooperation can make an effective and ",["timely response difficult","https://www.europol.europa.eu/publications-events/publications/seizing-opportunity-five-recommendations-for-crypto-assets-related-crime-and-money-laundering#downloads"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing North Korean cyber operations completely may be unrealistic. But there are several ways to make these activities less profitable and more difficult to carry out. These include strengthening identity verification procedures to prevent North Korean IT workers from gaining employment with false identities."]},{"k":"p","s":["They also include improving information-sharing between governments and private companies and enhancing cyber resilience. This would minimise the damage to targeted organisations and help them recover more quickly when attacks occur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, the goal should not only be to prevent attacks, but also to disrupt the networks that enable them, limit the financial gains and reduce their impact."]}],"chars":6099},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lithuania":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"20eb8367d03fe0043ff10f41325c55d7a23ac64301196c74596f4b8875e4c951","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/lithuania","bytes":71980,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Lithuania travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:19:26+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lithuania/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Lithuania set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Lithuanian Embassy in the UK","https://uk.mfa.lt/uk/en/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lithuania follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa to the Schengen area, which includes Lithuania, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirements for ",["working in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-lithuania-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Lithuanian border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Lithuanian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or permit you need with the ",["Lithuanian Embassy in the UK","https://uk.mfa.lt/uk/en/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay in Lithuania with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-lithuania#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arriving from Belarus or Russia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in Lithuania from Belarus or Russia, including the Kaliningrad Oblast, and need help, call +370 5246 2900 and select ‘calling about an emergency involving a British national’. You can also ",["contact FCDO online","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/lithuania/british-embassy-vilnius"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals can travel to Lithuania from Belarus or Russia by bus. Restrictions may apply if arriving in a privately owned car registered in Belarus. Russian plated vehicles are currently only permitted to enter Lithuania for up to 24 hours if transiting to or from the Kaliningrad Oblast."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, see the ",["Lithuanian Customs Service website","https://lrmuitine.lt/web/guest/naujienos/aktualijos/aktualija?p_p_id=EXT_WPLISTALLNEWS&p_p_lifecycle=0&_EXT_WPLISTALLNEWS_obj_id=090004d2801f1006#en"],", and read FCDO’s ",["Russia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/russia/returning-to-the-uk"]," or ",["Belarus travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belarus"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Belarus-Lithuania border closures"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 29 October 2025, Lithuania announced the closure of its border with Belarus until at least 30 November 2025. However, UK nationals are exempt and can continue to cross the border. For further information on these restrictions, see the ",["Lithuanian Government website","https://vrm.lrv.lt/en/news/lithuanian-government-have-decided-to-close-salcininkai-and-medininkai-border-checkpoints-with-belarus-for-one-month-4zSU/"]," (only available in Lithuanian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only one border crossing point between Lithuania and Belarus remains open: Medininkai-Kamenny Log. Crossing the border is only possible by private vehicle; scheduled buses are currently not operating across the Belarusian-Lithuanian border."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lithuania also denies entry to cars registered in Belarus, with certain exemptions. For further information on these restrictions, see ",["the Lithuanian Government website","https://muitine.lrv.lt/lt/naujienos/lengvuju-automobiliu-su-baltarusiskais-registracijos-numeriais-ivaziavimas-i-lietuva/"]," (only available in Lithuanian)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checkpoints on the Lithuania/Poland Border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Poland has reintroduced border checks on the Lithuania/Poland border. Vehicles may be stopped and documentation checked. For further information see ",["Poland Travel Advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Lithuania guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/131/lithuania#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Lithuania","https://lrmuitine.lt/web/guest/verslui/apribojimai/bendra#en"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Lithuania"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Lithuania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Russian vehicle restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ",["restrictions on vehicles with Russian number plates","https://lrmuitine.lt/web/guest/naujienos/aktualijos/aktualija?p_p_id=EXT_WPLISTALLNEWS&p_p_lifecycle=0&_EXT_WPLISTALLNEWS_obj_id=090004d2801c0364#en"]," in Lithuania."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Lithuania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Lithuania cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petty crime is common. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["beware of pickpockets in busy locations and on public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid unlit streets and parks at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["be cautious if you’re walking alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave coats and handbags unattended in bars, pubs and clubs"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been instances of drink spiking in Vilnius and at festivals and events elsewhere in Lithuania. Do not leave drinks unattended and be wary of accepting food and drink from strangers in bars, nightclubs and restaurants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, are strictly prohibited, even in very small quantities. Severe penalties apply for possessing, using, buying, or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports. You should expect long jail sentences of up to 10 years and heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Lithuania have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["While there are some LGBT+ friendly venues in larger cities, small towns and rural areas can be less accepting of LGBT+ travellers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal and same-sex partners can live together, but same-sex marriages and civil partnerships are not recognised under Lithuanian law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Lithuania, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Lithuania guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/lithuania/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other requirements that you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Lithuania. Make sure it has the correct name and address. ",["Renew or update your licence","https://www.gov.uk/renew-driving-licence"]," if necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Lithuania, and the ",["legal limits are stricter than in the UK","https://policija.lrv.lt/en/road-traffic-safety/excerpts-from-the-lithuanian-road-traffic-rules/e-driving-under-the-influence-of-drugs/"],". If you are tested and have over the legal limit for alcohol in your system, you may face a heavy fine and imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is safer to use a recognised taxi app or to phone for a registered taxi that uses a meter. Make sure the meter is switched on to avoid arguments about the fare."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drone activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Ukrainian drones aimed at Russia have crossed into Lithuanian airspace. Follow official guidance as necessary."]},{"k":"h","s":["Curonian Spit, Klaipeda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Spit, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is divided between Lithuania and Russia – the northern half is in Lithuania and the southern half is part of Kaliningrad, Russia. Visitors should be aware that the walk along the Curonian Spit in Lithuanian territory will eventually reach Russian territory. See ",["Russia travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/russia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Lithuania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/131/lithuania#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Lithuania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/131/lithuania"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Lithuania"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lithuania-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Lithuania, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-lithuania#healthcare"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Lithuania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Lithuania"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Lithuania"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Lithuania"]," in Lithuania"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lithuania-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/prisoner-pack-lithuania"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/lithuania/british-embassy-vilnius"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lithuania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Lithuania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-lithuania"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15858,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/nz-has-unique-stories-of-evolution-and-geology-is-it-time-for-a-natural-history-museum-292115":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"cea0fce41ab01181b2f2beb2137ed1bb1df745e35b19d92283abbfc8c1680ef8","read":"https://theconversation.com/nz-has-unique-stories-of-evolution-and-geology-is-it-time-for-a-natural-history-museum-292115","bytes":186101,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"NZ has unique stories of evolution and geology. Is it time for a natural history museum?","by":[{"n":"Nic Rawlence","r":"Associate Professor in Ancient DNA, University of Otago"}],"pub":"2026-11-08T23:46:44Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Like the Galapagos Islands, New Zealand’s unique isolation makes it an iconic natural history location of global importance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Already famous for its flightless birds and their story of evolution on a mammal-free archipelago, New Zealand is home to many other, less well known but equally important plants and animals."]},{"k":"p","s":["This includes ",["horopito","https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora/species/pseudowintera-colorata/"],", which has the most primitive flower of any plant alive today, or the ",["hihi/stitchbird","https://www.nzbirdsonline.org.nz/species/stitchbird"],", which is the only member of an entire avian family."]},{"k":"p","s":["I often wonder why New Zealand doesn’t have a dedicated natural history museum (like those in ",["London","https://www.nhm.ac.uk/"],", ",["Paris","https://www.mnhn.fr/en"],", ",["Vienna","https://www.nhm.at/en/"]," or ",["New York","https://www.amnh.org/"],") to celebrate its unique biodiversity, geology and fossil record."]},{"k":"p","s":["With ",["ongoing changes","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/community/1058389/te-papa-chief-executive-courtney-johnston-announces-resignation"]," in leadership at the ",["Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa","https://www.tepapa.govt.nz/"],", it might be time to have this conversation."]},{"k":"h","s":["The case for a natural history museum"]},{"k":"p","s":["The research of ",["natural history scientists at Te Papa","https://www.tepapa.govt.nz/learn/research/natural-history-research/natural-history-team"]," is ",["world class","https://theconversation.com/empty-mollusc-shells-hold-the-story-of-evolution-even-for-extinct-species-now-we-can-decode-it-187927"],". But in terms of public-facing displays, the museum cannot do New Zealand’s geological and biological heritage justice."]},{"k":"p","s":["It has to be too many things to too many people, leaving too little space for natural history."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some treasures are currently on display, including New Zealand’s ",["first dinosaur fossil","https://www.rnz.co.nz/national/programmes/ourchangingworld/audio/2599964/joan-wiffen-and-her-dinosaurs"]," discovered by famed ",["palaeontologist Joan Wiffen","https://collections.tepapa.govt.nz/topic/1326"],". But this and other fossils of national and global significance remain mostly confined to a small exhibition area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only a tiny fraction of any museum’s collections is on display. Notable examples missing from display at Te Papa include reconstructions of New Zealand’s dinosaurs and many fossils of recently discovered species such as the eight-million-year-old ",["giant crab","https://www.nzgeo.com/stories/crushing-it/"]," from Taranaki."]},{"k":"p","s":["Apart from Te Papa’s collections, Wellington holds others of national importance, including of ",["fossils","https://www.earthsciences.nz/about-us/celebrating-100-years-of-science/time-travellers-boost-research"],", ",["marine species","https://niwa.co.nz/oceans/earth-sciences-new-zealand-invertebrate-collection"]," and ",["rocks","https://www.gns.cri.nz/data-and-resources/national-petrology-reference-collection/"]," at ",["Earth Sciences New Zealand","https://www.earthsciences.nz/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Around the country, other collections also exist, including of arthropods and fungi as well as the ",["Allan Herbarium","https://www.landcareresearch.co.nz/tools-and-resources/collections/allan-herbarium"]," at the ",["Bioeconomy Science Institute","https://www.landcareresearch.co.nz/tools-and-resources/collections"],". The University of Otago’s ",["geology museum","https://www.otago.ac.nz/geology/about/museum"]," is an example of a collection held by an academic institution."]},{"k":"p","s":["But these collections aren’t protected by an act of parliament like Te Papa, and they don’t have the same level of public accessibility or funding the national museum has. I propose they should all be combined to form the basis of a new museum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Current public displays on New Zealand’s biodiversity don’t always put it into a global or evolutionary context. For example, New Zealand is the ",["cradle of penguin evolution","https://theconversation.com/dagger-beaks-and-strong-wings-new-fossils-rewrite-the-penguin-story-and-affirm-nz-as-a-cradle-of-their-evolution-261083"]," and the ancestors of many now endemic birds came from ",["Australia","https://theconversation.com/loss-of-forests-brought-new-birds-to-nz-during-the-last-ice-age-were-witnessing-a-similar-process-now-248523"],", ",["South America","https://blogs.otago.ac.nz/lost-worlds/2022/03/28/the-long-night-how-the-ice-age-drove-blue-eyed-shag-evolution/"],", the ",["northern hemisphere","https://theconversation.com/ancient-dna-from-an-extinct-native-duck-reveals-how-far-birds-flew-to-make-new-zealand-home-229117"]," and in some cases, ",["places unknown","https://theconversation.com/are-kiwi-and-moa-recent-immigrants-from-australia-neither-fossils-nor-genetic-evidence-support-the-story-238577"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Biodiversity displays could be further strengthened by showcasing New Zealand’s geological heritage. Rock and mineral displays can be ",["popular attractions","https://www.smithsonianmag.com/blogs/national-museum-of-natural-history/2023/06/28/new-museum-display-showcases-the-mineral-building-blocks-of-cellphones/"]," and it would be a prime opportunity to put pounamu in a global context. Pounamu is the Indigenous Māori name for ",["nephrite jade and bowenite","https://www.earthsciences.nz/news/pounamu-toughest-stone-of-its-kind-in-the-world"],", which is a taonga (treasure) for carving."]},{"k":"h","s":["From contested to globally relevant spaces"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Victorian concept of a museum has a colonial history. This has led to collections containing numerous ",["contested objects","https://www.abc.net.au/listen/programs/stuff-the-british-stole"]," such as the ",["Parthenon marbles","https://theconversation.com/the-parthenon-marbles-evoke-particularly-fierce-repatriation-debates-an-archaeologist-explains-why-219152"]," in the British Museum and Indigenous human remains stored in collections worldwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["By being open about this history and working with mana whenua (local Māori groups), a new museum could help heal these rifts."]},{"k":"p","s":["This would enable exhibitions with a global focus, for example about the evolution of life on Earth, to be told through the fossil record and living biodiversity."]},{"k":"p","s":["A prime example is the fossil of one of the first dinosaurs ever described ( ",["Iguanodon","https://www.liverpoolmuseums.org.uk/stories/200-years-of-iguanodon-focus"],"), ",["held by Te Papa","https://collections.tepapa.govt.nz/object/212194?page=1&rtp=1&ros=1&asr=1&assoc=all&mb=c"],", which helped start the world’s ongoing interest in dinosaurs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Currently Te Papa does not display any biodiversity from outside New Zealand. Imagine seeing a whole gallery of fossil and living whale skeletons to illustrate their remarkable evolutionary journey from land to sea, similar to displays in the ",["gallery of palaeontology and comparative anatomy","https://www.mnhn.fr/en/galerie-de-paleontologie-et-d-anatomie-comparee-paleontology-and-comparative-anatomy-gallery"]," in Paris."]},{"k":"p","s":["Like the incredible, almost complete ",["Triceratops skeleton","https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2020/dec/02/melbourne-museum-acquires-worlds-most-complete-triceratops-skeleton-in-immense-dinosaur-deal"]," ",["Museums Victoria","https://museumsvictoria.com.au/melbournemuseum/"]," acquired for AU$3 million, a dedicated natural history museum in New Zealand should source specimens and loans ethically to promote collaborative research and public outreach."]},{"k":"p","s":["Scientists and their research could also be showcased. This would keep the museum relevant and in the public mind. As part of its public exhibitions, the ",["Swedish Museum of Natural History","https://www.nrm.se/engelska/in-english"]," has displays of their researchers explaining the importance of their work."]},{"k":"h","s":["Location, support and funding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Core activities of a natural history museum include growing, caring for and researching collections as well as providing access to the public. Most of these are not financially viable."]},{"k":"p","s":["A natural history museum would therefore require core funding from central government to ",["avoid closure","https://www.npr.org/2026/10/03/nx-s1-5989716/philadelphia-academy-natural-sciences-museum-closure"]," such as what recently happened at the Philadelphia Academy of Natural Sciences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public-private partnerships are a funding option but have raised ethical issues such as the London Science Museum’s ",["past relationship with the oil company Equinor","https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/aug/28/london-science-museum-cuts-links-with-bp-after-decades-of-partnership"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["A new museum may seem expensive, but it could generate significant tourism income to reinvest into curation and research. Museums in New Zealand contributed at least ",["NZ$1.1 billion to New Zealand’s GDP","https://berl.co.nz/our-mahi/economic-impact-museums-and-galleries"]," in 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["High-quality international touring exhibitions, such as Te Papa’s successful ",["Whales Tohora","https://www.tepapa.govt.nz/about/touring-exhibitions/past-touring-exhibitions/whales-tohora"],", could further showcase the global importance of New Zealand’s biological heritage."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Gareth Nelson","https://asbs.org.au/grants-awards/gareth-nelson-award/"],", who was the curator of fishes at the American Museum of Natural History before retiring to Australia to work on plant taxonomy, once famously said:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Explain New Zealand and the world falls into place around it."]},{"k":"p","s":["This could be the guiding principle for a new museum dedicated to New Zealand’s biological heritage."]}],"chars":5751},"https://theconversation.com/midterms-are-bad-for-incumbents-and-even-worse-when-energy-prices-are-high-295287":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"345d49590f0b2477dd7b6280dddaebd2a50bcbb1664bd685426791c0275d60b8","read":"https://theconversation.com/midterms-are-bad-for-incumbents-and-even-worse-when-energy-prices-are-high-295287","bytes":191779,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Midterms are bad for incumbents – and even worse when energy prices are high","by":[{"n":"Michael A. Mische","r":"Associate Professor of the Practice of Management and Organization, Marshall School of Business, University of Southern California"}],"pub":"2026-11-04T19:06:28Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["As Democrats and Republicans look at the overwhelming results of the 2026 midterm election, it’s worth remembering what has become a political axiom in America: “ ",["It’s the economy, stupid","https://politicaldictionary.com/words/its-the-economy-stupid/"],".” Democratic strategist James Carville famously said that to presidential candidate Bill Clinton in 1992, but he might have said “it’s energy prices” instead. ",["The cost of energy underlies much of the economy","https://theconversation.com/iran-war-pushes-diesel-the-economys-lifeblood-to-record-high-prices-with-no-relief-on-the-horizon-292049"],", making energy and politics inseparable, especially when gasoline prices rise."]},{"k":"p","s":["Midterm elections have historically been ",["difficult for incumbent presidents","https://doi.org/10.1177/1532673X251325458"]," and ",["often shift","https://www.scrippsnews.com/politics/midterm-elections/why-does-the-president-s-party-typically-lose-midterms"]," the ",["balance of power","https://riponsociety.org/article/the-midterm-curse-and-the-balance-of-power-in-washington/"]," in Washington, D.C."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many factors affecting gasoline prices are beyond a president’s or Congress’s control. Prices for crude oil and petroleum ",["products such as gasoline","https://pumptex.com/6-interesting-facts-about-gas-stations.php"]," are ",["set on global markets","https://www.investopedia.com/articles/economics/08/determining-oil-prices.asp"]," as the results of economic forces of supply and demand. Even the companies that produce oil don’t have ",["as much influence as people might think","https://www.afpm.org/newsroom/blog/do-refineries-set-price-gasoline"],", because of how that oil gets to refineries: Over 60% of the world’s crude oil is ",["transported by ocean tankers","https://understand-energy.stanford.edu/news/understand-oil-trade-and-transportation"],", with 20% of global supplies ",["traveling through the Strait of Hormuz","https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=65504"],", which has been closed, or nearly so, for much of 2026 as the conflict with Iran drags on."]},{"k":"p","s":["When ",["energy prices rise, other prices, such as food","https://theconversation.com/iran-war-pushes-diesel-the-economys-lifeblood-to-record-high-prices-with-no-relief-on-the-horizon-292049"],", follow. ",["Sudden spikes in gasoline prices","https://www.dallasfed.org/-/media/documents/research/papers/2022/wp2224.pdf"]," can contribute to ",["higher inflation, both regionally","https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/inflationary-impact-energy-prices"]," ",["and nationally","https://nypost.com/2026/10/29/business/feds-preferred-inflation-gauge-heats-up-over-high-gas-prices/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Voters pay attention","https://doi.org/10.1177/1532673X251325458"]," to those changes, and ",["incumbents are less likely to win reelection","https://www.spglobal.com/energy/en/news-research/latest-news/crude-oil/062624-us-elections-gasoline-price-fluctuations-could-play-role-in-2024-presidential-election"],". For the 2026 midterm election, ",["gasoline prices were the highest","https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/11/02/gas-prices-are-set-be-highest-any-election-day-us-history/"]," of any previous election. That put Republicans in the precarious position of ",["defending their record","https://thehill.com/policy/energy-environment/6173484-republicans-high-gas-prices-voters-midterms"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Four American presidents – Gerald Ford, Jimmy Carter, Ronald Reagan and Joe Biden – confronted the ",["consequences of severe inflation and high fuel prices","https://grist.org/politics/jimmy-carter-legacy-energy-american-politics/"]," during midterm elections."]},{"k":"h","s":["Oil embargo, Nixon and Ford"]},{"k":"p","s":["Richard Nixon was the first modern president to truly face an energy crisis that became political. In retaliation for U.S. support for Israel during the October 1973 Yom Kippur War, Arab members of the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries ",["cut oil production and imposed an oil embargo","https://history.state.gov/milestones/1969-1976/oil-embargo"]," on the United States. ",["OPEC oil production fell by 5% a month","https://www.bakerinstitute.org/research/arab-embargo-50-years-ago-weaponized-oil-inflict-economic-trauma-sound-familiar"],", and crude oil prices rocketed 184% from prewar levels of ",["$4.31 to $10.31 per barrel","https://www.macrotrends.net/1369/crude-oil-price-history-chart"]," in March 1974. Nixon’s ",["federal price controls on petroleum","https://www.congress.gov/bill/93rd-congress/house-bill/8863"]," didn’t prevent U.S. ",["gasoline prices from increasing 32%","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=197301&end=202609&charted=5-10-11"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["When Nixon resigned over the Watergate scandal in August 1974, Gerald Ford took office. ",["Inflation was 12.3%","https://www.investopedia.com/inflation-rate-by-year-7253832"],", and ",["gas prices were still high","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=197301&end=202609&charted=5-10-11"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Right before that year’s midterm election, Ford launched the “ ",["Whip Inflation Now","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/win-how-gerald-ford-tried-to-whip-inflation-with-a-button/"],",” or WIN, campaign. But ",["Republicans lost 48 House seats","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"]," and five Senate seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["“WIN” didn’t work, and by the 1976 presidential election, gas prices were ",["over 60 cents a gallon","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=197507&end=197611&charted=5-10-11"]," – adjusted for inflation to late 2026, that’s $3.49. Ford lost his reelection bid to Jimmy Carter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Carter’s struggles"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Carter’s first two years in office, starting in 1977, the monthly average price of unleaded gasoline in the U.S. ",["stayed high and even climbed slightly","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=197612&end=198101&charted=5-10-11"],". Inflation hit ",["9% in 1978","https://www.investopedia.com/inflation-rate-by-year-7253832"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 1978 midterm election, ",["Democrats lost 15 House and three Senate seats","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"],". ",["Inflation continued to climb","https://www.investopedia.com/inflation-rate-by-year-7253832"],", and by the 1980 presidential election, gas prices were ",["twice what they had been in 1976","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=197507&end=197611&charted=5-10-11"],". Plagued by those figures and the Iranian hostage crisis, Carter lost the 1980 election to Ronald Reagan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Reagan enters the picture"]},{"k":"p","s":["Reagan implemented “ ",["Reaganomics","https://www.law.georgetown.edu/denny-center/blog/reaganomics/"],"” by cutting taxes and regulations, reducing government spending, tightening monetary policy and ",["removing the remaining price controls on petroleum","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-12287-decontrol-crude-oil-and-refined-petroleum-products"],". By the mid-1980s, ",["increased oil production from U.S.","https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/leafhandler.ashx?n=pet&s=mcrfpus2&f=m"]," and non-OPEC nations ",["led to an oil glut","https://www.nytimes.com/1981/06/21/business/how-the-oil-glut-is-changing-business.html"],", lowering the ",["average price of crude oil","https://www.macrotrends.net/1369/crude-oil-price-history-chart"]," and ",["U.S. gasoline price from previous highs","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=198009&end=198902&charted=5-10-11"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 1982 midterms, ",["Republicans lost 26 seats in the House","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"]," and gained one in the Senate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reagan won reelection to the presidency in a landslide in 1984, but the challenges for incumbents remained in the 1986 midterms. Though ",["crude oil prices were $15 a barrel","https://www.macrotrends.net/1369/crude-oil-price-history-chart"]," and ",["gas had dropped to 82 cents","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=198009&end=198902&charted=5-10-11"]," a gallon, ",["Republicans lost five seats in the House","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"]," and eight in the Senate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Trump’s first round"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the lead-up to the midterms during Donald Trump’s first term as president, crude prices had ",["risen about 24%","https://www.macrotrends.net/1369/crude-oil-price-history-chart"]," from when he took office in January 2017 to October 2018. And ",["gas prices were up 22%","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/monthly/index.php"],". In the 2018 midterms, Republicans ",["lost 41 House seats but gained two in the Senate","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Biden years"]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the course of 2020, COVID-19 restrictions slowed the U.S. economy. ",["U.S. crude oil production fell","https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/leafhandler.ashx?n=pet&s=mcrfpus2&f=m"]," as ",["gasoline demand plummeted by 40%","https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=46141"],". Prices rose because of pandemic-related supply chain backups."]},{"k":"p","s":["And from Election Day in November 2020 to Russia’s invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, the average price of unleaded gasoline in the U.S. rose by 66%, ",["from $2.11 to $3.52 per gallon","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=200001"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Also, as pandemic restrictions lifted and the economy began recovering, demand for gasoline rebounded, straining supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Upon taking office in 2021, Biden took steps to curb rising energy costs, including ",["releasing oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve","https://www.bbc.com/news/business-60936468"]," in March 2022, which the Treasury Department suggested helped prevent gasoline price increases of ",["$0.17 to $0.42 per gallon","https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0887"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But other Biden policy moves made it harder to increase energy supplies. He ",["canceled the Keystone XL pipeline project","https://www.cnbc.com/2021/06/09/tc-energy-terminates-keystone-xl-pipeline-project.html"]," that would have brought more petroleum into the U.S. and ",["suspended new oil and gas leases","https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/LSB11259"]," in the Arctic National Wildlife Refuge and the Gulf of Mexico. He also ",["recommitted the U.S. to the Paris climate accord","https://2021-2025.state.gov/the-united-states-officially-rejoins-the-paris-agreement/"],", under which countries have promised to cut their greenhouse gas emissions, generally meaning moving away from fossil fuels as an energy source."]},{"k":"p","s":["In June 2022, ",["inflation reached 9.1%","https://www.investopedia.com/us-inflation-rate-by-president-8546447"],", a 40-year high. And U.S. gasoline prices reached an ",["all-time high of $4.929 per gallon","https://www.eia.gov/totalenergy/data/browser/index.php?tbl=T09.04#/?f=M&start=200001"],"; adjusted for inflation, that’s $5.60 a gallon today."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 2022 midterm election wasn’t as bad for Democrats as they might have feared, though it wasn’t a success: The party ",["lost nine House seats","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/seats-congress-gainedlost-the-presidents-party-mid-term-elections"]," and one Senate seat. That’s a reminder that ",["energy prices aren’t the only factor","https://news.stanford.edu/stories/2022/10/drives-american-voters"]," in voters’ minds when they are casting ballots."]},{"k":"h","s":["Trump’s second term"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the first 12 months of Trump’s second term, ",["crude oil prices fell 4.5%","https://www.macrotrends.net/1369/crude-oil-price-history-chart"],", U.S. ",["oil production rose 3.3%","https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/leafhandler.ashx?n=pet&s=mcrfpus2&f=m"],", from 13.3 million to 13.7 million barrels per day, and the AAA national average price of regular unleaded gasoline fell 4.5%, ",["from $3.12","https://gasprices.aaa.com/2025/02/"]," to ",["$2.98 per gallon","https://gasprices.aaa.com/2026/02/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Feb. 28, 2026, U.S. military action against Iran disrupted Middle Eastern oil production and oil tanker traffic in the Strait of Hormuz. Initially, ",["shipment volume plummeted","https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/01/crude-oil-exports-strait-of-hormuz-transport-gulf-region-diesel"],", though by the end of September it had ",["recovered to 82% to 92% of prewar levels","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/30/iran-war-strait-hormuz-gulf-oil-fuel.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overall, Middle Eastern crude oil exports are averaging around 24 million barrels a day, ",["exceeding prewar levels","https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/more-oil-is-now-coming-out-of-the-persian-gulf-than-before-the-iran-war-6a6d1670"]," in part because of increased use of pipelines out of Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates. Because of the war with Iran, AAA’s national average price of unleaded regular gasoline has increased by almost 40%, from ",["February’s $2.98 price","https://gasprices.aaa.com/2026/01/"]," to ",["$4.15 a gallon","https://gasprices.aaa.com/"]," as of Nov. 3, 2026."]},{"k":"h","s":["Implications"]},{"k":"p","s":["As the preelection polling had suggested, voters held Trump accountable for ",["high gasoline and grocery prices","https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3956"],", as well as ",["an unpopular war","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/08/iran-conflict-remains-deeply-unpopular-as-many-americans-expect-it-to-go-on-for-months/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was a reminder of a basic economic and political principle: When the economy is doing well, ",["voters are more likely to support incumbents","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electstud.2010.09.001"]," and their parties. And when voters are ",["pessimistic about the economy’s future","https://www.cnbc.com/guide/midterm-elections-economy-affordability/"],", they are ",["inclined to vote against incumbents","https://doi.org/10.1111/0022-3816.00063"]," and their parties."]}],"chars":7477},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"c6b385345953610395ab8a9cc21cea5a0c1ff6b789a230eba16f46d2cd1aaa15","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe","bytes":73424,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Zimbabwe travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-15T09:15:29+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Zimbabwe’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Zimbabwe set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Zimbabwean Embassy in the UK","https://www.facebook.com/zimembassylondon/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Zimbabwe, your passport must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive"]},{"k":"li","s":["3 blank pages, in case you need to enter Zimbabwe and exit through one of the neighbouring countries or if you need to leave at short notice"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet their requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Zimbabwe. Most visitors get their visa on arrival."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["The visa on arrival is usually granted for 30 days. Take enough US dollars with you in small notes to pay for your visa. See ",["information on visa fees from the Zimbabwean Embassy","https://www.evisa.gov.zw/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is possible to ",["apply for an e-visa","https://www.evisa.gov.zw/index.html"]," before you travel, with options for single entry or double entry visas at different prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also use the KAZA Univisa in Zimbabwe. It is valid for travel between Zimbabwe and Zambia and for day trips into Botswana. The KAZA Univisa is available at Harare, Bulawayo and Victoria Falls airports and at the land borders at Victoria Falls (Zimbabwe-Zambia border) and Kazungula (Zimbabwe-Botswana border). It costs 50 US dollars and is valid for 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is no longer possible to get a visa from the Zimbabwean Embassy in London."]},{"k":"p","s":["To extend or renew visas or permits, go in person to the Government of Zimbabwe Immigration Department."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer or to work or study, or for business travel, you must meet the Zimbabwean government’s entry requirements. You must have a temporary work permit if you’re volunteering or doing missionary work."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Zimbabwean temporary travel documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwean temporary travel documents (TTDs) are not valid for re-entry to the UK. You could be stranded in Zimbabwe if you travel using this document."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Zimbabwe, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Zimbabwe guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/248/zimbabwe#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods that you can take into or out of Zimbabwe. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Arms embargo"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a UK arms embargo against Zimbabwe. It is an offence in UK law to take firearms into Zimbabwe, even if you plan to bring them back to the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gemstones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not carry any precious or semi-precious stones without the correct paperwork."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pornographic material"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to carry or import pornographic material."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Zimbabwe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. It is illegal to leave Zimbabwe with cash worth more than 2,000 US dollars."]},{"k":"h","s":["Journalists"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re working as a journalist (for example, as a reporter or news photographer), you must get accreditation before you travel from the ",["Zimbabwean Embassy in the UK","https://www.facebook.com/zimembassylondon/"],". If you do not have proper accreditation, you risk arrest, detention in difficult conditions, a fine and deportation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Zimbabwe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Zimbabwe, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations and rallies can be unpredictable and may turn violent. Authorities have in the past used force to suppress them. Avoid political gatherings or activities which could be considered political, including political discussions in public places or online."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to make derogatory or insulting comments about the President or to carry material considered to be offensive towards the office of President."]},{"k":"h","s":["Blackouts and water rationing"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent, and sometimes long, power blackouts because of electricity shortages. During blackouts, traffic lights may not work. There is also water rationing in parts of the country. Contact your tour operator or hotel for the latest updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mobile network and landlines"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Zimbabwean mobile phone network and landlines are unreliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a moderate level of crime in Zimbabwe. People travelling alone may be more vulnerable. Mugging, pickpocketing and bag-snatching are common in city centres, especially after dark. Street lighting can be poor. Be vigilant when leaving banks and ATMs. Do not carry or display large amounts of cash in public places."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been occasional armed robberies targeting foreign residents. Make sure your accommodation is always secure."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been smash-and-grab robberies from vehicles, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["at the main intersections along the route to Robert Gabriel Mugabe International Airport"]},{"k":"li","s":["along Liberation Legacy Way (Borrowdale Road) and Churchill Road in Harare"]},{"k":"li","s":["on the Masvingo-Beitbridge road"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly vigilant when using these routes. Keep vehicle doors locked and windows closed. Be careful at night and at petrol stations. Do not leave your vehicle parked – even for a short time – in unguarded areas in towns."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry a copy of your passport’s photo page and your visa at all times. Leave your original passport somewhere safe. If you lose your UK passport, get a police report. You may need to show this to immigration to explain why you have no proof of entry when you depart."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwean residents must carry their residence card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Zimbabwe have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwe’s economy is unpredictable. Monetary policy can change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwe has a multi-currency system. You can use US dollars for most transactions. In April 2024, Zimbabwe Gold (ZiG) was introduced as a new currency to replace the Zimbabwean dollar. The US dollar remains legal tender."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to exchange foreign currency anywhere other than at officially licensed dealers such as banks or bureaux de change. Bureaux de change will accept and change foreign currency, particularly US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a shortage of physical US dollar cash, so it’s not always possible to make withdrawals using an international debit or credit card. Change is rarely available, so carry small denomination notes. Do not accept torn or damaged notes in change as shops and restaurants are likely to refuse them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check in advance what payment methods a restaurant, hotel or tour operator will accept. Some businesses, including some medical providers, may not accept credit or debit cards. Most suppliers prefer US dollars in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["International money transfers from outside Zimbabwe are not always successful."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs of government offices, airports, military establishments, political party offices, official residences, embassies and other sensitive locations without special permission from the Ministry of Information. It is also illegal to photograph police and armed forces personnel, demonstrations and protests. The police strictly enforce these laws. You should exercise caution and avoid taking photos or videos that might accidentally include sensitive buildings or personnel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["State House in Harare"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed members of the Presidential Guard patrol the area around State House in Harare (the President’s official residence). They do not allow loitering by motorists, cyclists or pedestrians, and it is illegal to take photographs. The roads in this area are closed from 6pm to 6am. Do not use GPS navigation systems around the President’s residence and, if possible, avoid the area altogether."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Journalism and social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Zimbabwean government uses a broad definition of journalism. This may include any form of interview, filming or photography. Journalism is illegal without accreditation. See ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe/entry-requirements#journalists"],". Consider carefully the risks of any social media activities, including posting comments, blogging or sharing photographs, which can be seen as journalism."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwe’s position on dual nationality has been inconsistent. The Constitutional Court has ruled that some categories of dual nationality are legal, and that Zimbabwean citizens by birth may hold dual nationality. However, Zimbabwean law prohibits dual citizenship for those who acquire Zimbabwean citizenship by descent or registration. The authorities may obstruct, detain or even seek to prosecute someone they consider an offender."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national considering acquiring Zimbabwean citizenship, you should take legal advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. Buying or trafficking such items risks prosecution and a prison sentence of up to 9 years."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Camouflage clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for civilians to wear any form of clothing made from camouflage material."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sex between men and same-sex marriage are illegal in Zimbabwe. Zimbabwean society remains conservative towards same-sex relations, especially between men. However, there is a small but active underground LGBT+ scene in Harare and prosecutions are rare. Be aware that showing affection in public could result in unwanted attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],". You can also find more local information from the GALZ Association."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Safari lodges and game reserves"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards in Zimbabwe’s safari lodges and game reserves vary. Check with the ",["Safari Operators Association of Zimbabwe","https://www.facebook.com/p/Safari-Operators-Association-of-Zimbabwe-SOAZ-100067071251403/"]," whether operators are trained and licensed. Animal attacks have injured and killed visitors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Treat wild animals with caution and always keep a safe distance. Some activities, such as walking or canoe safaris, could pose risks to personal safety. Make sure your travel insurance covers all the activities you plan on doing in Zimbabwe."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Zimbabwe, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Zimbabwe with a UK driving licence for up to 12 months. Make sure you have copies of your passport’s photo page and visa with you in the car at all times. Be ready to show ID if asked and keep the originals in a safe place where you can get them easily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Obey police signals, stop at roadblocks and toll gates. Make sure you get a receipt if you have to pay a fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re resident in Zimbabwe, you may want to get a Zimbabwean licence to minimise the chance of problems at roadblocks."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re bringing a vehicle not registered in Zimbabwe into the country, you must have a police vehicle clearance certificate (temporary import permit)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of driving is very poor in Zimbabwe. Traffic accidents are a common cause of death and injury. Hazards include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["deep potholes"]},{"k":"li","s":["broken traffic lights"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicles without lights (including heavy good vehicles and cyclists)"]},{"k":"li","s":["poorly lit roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["badly marked roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["stray livestock"]},{"k":"li","s":["pedestrians"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency services may provide very limited help in the event of an accident and ambulances are unreliable."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["always wear a seatbelt"]},{"k":"li","s":["lock car doors"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid driving outside main towns at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel carefully on roads between cities"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry a comprehensive medical kit"]},{"k":"li","s":["be careful about stopping at laybys"]},{"k":"p","s":["Plan carefully before setting out on long-distance journeys. Get local advice about any places you plan to visit. Fuel is sometimes unavailable and there may be queues. Carry extra fuel and top up your tank whenever possible. Bring cash in case your bank card is not accepted."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to continue driving when the President’s motorcade goes past, no matter which side of the road you’re on. If you see the motorcade, pull off the road or on to the side of the road if this is not possible. The security forces have assaulted people for stopping in the wrong place or for not stopping soon enough."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Commuter buses (‘combis’) are often overcrowded, inadequately maintained, uninsured and recklessly driven. Avoid them if possible. Larger intercity buses may also be poorly driven. There have been serious road accidents involving long-distance buses travelling at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis recommended by hotels are usually reliable and in good condition. Major hotels usually have their own taxis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#zimbabwe"]," lists all known airlines in Zimbabwe that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to and from the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["British government employees travelling to and within Zimbabwe have been advised to use carriers that are not on the UK ASL."]},{"k":"p","s":["Air Zimbabwe has resumed direct flights between London and Harare. This service is operated by Spanish carrier Plus Ultra Líneas Aéreas on behalf of Air Zimbabwe. As Plus Ultra Líneas Aéreas is the operating carrier and holds the necessary approvals to operate services to the UK, this specific route is eligible under UK air safety regulations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rail system in Zimbabwe is underdeveloped and very poorly maintained. Level crossings are poorly marked, resulting in many accidents. Passenger services are currently suspended. Check with ",["National Railways of Zimbabwe","https://nrz.co.zw/"]," for updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently heavy rainfall and flooding across Southern Africa, including in areas of Zimbabwe. The rainy season runs from November to April. Heavy rainfall can damage roads, or make them impassable in some areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Zimbabwe. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rural areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["There continue to be occasional invasions of commercial farms, sometimes accompanied by violence and threats. Take care when visiting farming areas that you are not familiar with."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mining areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mining areas are often restricted. Turn back if you are stopped and told that you are not allowed to access a particular area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 from a mobile phone and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zimbabwe’s emergency response capabilities are limited and, in many places, you will need to make local arrangements for transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Official Government of Zimbabwe web portal has a full list of emergency numbers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Zimbabwe","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/248/zimbabwe#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["There are currently a number of disease outbreaks in Zimbabwe. For more information, please see ",["NaTHNaC - Zimbabwe","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/248/zimbabwe#Outbreaks"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Zimbabwe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare provision and quality in Zimbabwe is variable and can be very poor outside of the major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are shortages of drugs and trained medical staff in hospitals, making it difficult for hospitals to treat some illnesses and trauma cases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency response capabilities are limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private clinics will not treat patients until they pay and often require large amounts of cash before they will admit emergency cases, even if you have travel insurance. Many businesses in Zimbabwe will only accept US dollars in cash, rather than credit or debit cards. This includes some medical providers. Medical costs, particularly for evacuation, can be high. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/zimbabwe-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where most staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Zimbabwe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Econet (mobile service provider) subscribers: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["NetOne (mobile service provider) subscribers: 114"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landline: 0800 3222 911"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Official Government of Zimbabwe web portal has a full list of local emergency numbers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Zimbabwe"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Zimbabwe"]," in Zimbabwe"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["help and services in Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/world/zimbabwe"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-zimbabwe"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/zimbabwe-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/zimbabwe/british-embassy-harare"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zimbabwe/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Zimbabwe","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-zimbabwe"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21109,"change":"Addition of information about direct flights between London and Harare ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/strict-liability-the-legal-standard-that-could-help-rein-in-ai-295390":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T20:22Z","sha":"1425e7890318b0165688edd02193863a9f7ba96e5b1848b627654e16d1549061","read":"https://theconversation.com/strict-liability-the-legal-standard-that-could-help-rein-in-ai-295390","bytes":182543,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Strict liability’: The legal standard that could help rein in AI","by":[{"n":"Deven Desai","r":"Professor of Business Law and Ethics; Associate Director for Law, Policy, and Ethics at the Machine Learning Center, Georgia Institute of Technology"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:41:07Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Some people have begun using the legal system to rein in AI companies and the harms they are creating. Cases are mounting."]},{"k":"p","s":["In October 2026, the parents of Bowen Wan sued OpenAI, charging that it’s ChatGPT agent may have instructed their daughter to ",["stop taking her medication, leading to her death","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/27/well/ai-chatgpt-medication-epilepsy-death.html"],". In 2024, a mother sued the Character.AI company, claiming that its chatbot’s interactions with her son ",["contributed to his suicide","https://www.reuters.com/legal/mother-sues-ai-chatbot-company-characterai-google-sued-over-sons-suicide-2024-10-23/"],". The state of Kentucky later ",["filed suit","https://www.wlky.com/article/unredacted-kentucky-ai-chatbot-lawsuit-louisville/74099366"],", claiming that Character.AI’s software exposed minors to self-harm and psychological manipulation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Social media companies, powered by artificial intelligence, are also ",["facing lawsuits about injuries","https://www.mofo.com/resources/insights/250618-software-gains-new-status-as-a-product-under-strict-liability-law"]," they purportedly caused."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regulating AI was ",["a hot issue","https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-intelligence/ai-tech-brief/2026/11/04/ai-tech-brief-midterms-turn-ai-tide/"]," during the 2026 midterms, too. ",["Several candidates","https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/2026/11/04/democrats-promise-ai-regulation-in-new-congress/92612851007/"]," who won their races have a ",["regulation agenda","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/04/democrats-eye-a-silicon-valley-ai-reckoning-01148624"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am ",["a former litigator and","https://www.scheller.gatech.edu/directory/faculty/desai/index.html"]," ",["a professor of business law","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=NVmtt8UAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"],", and all this action signals to me that people are looking to the law to protect them from AI harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["But what is the legal liability of AI software? An answer may be found in a principle known as ",["strict liability","https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/strict_liability"],". Applied properly, strict liability could restrain the risky parts of the AI industry and still allow it to provide the tools the public wants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Abnormally dangerous software"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tort law protects people from negligence, such as ",["who is responsible if you slip and fall in a store","https://www.justia.com/injury/negligence-theory/actual-and-proximate-cause/"],". Strict liability is part of tort law, but it is used to hold a person or company responsible for harm even if they were not at fault, not negligent or had no intent of creating trouble."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two types of strict liability matter for AI. One addresses ",["abnormally dangerous activity","https://opencasebook.org/casebooks/4643-tobia-torts-2022/resources/9.2.4-restatement-3d-liability-for-physical-and-emotional-harm-20-abnormally-dangerous-activities/"],", such as blasting with dynamite or transporting radioactive material. The other addresses ",["when a product hurts someone using it","https://www.nycbar.org/get-legal-help/article/personal-injury-and-accidents/product-liability/examples-cases-can-result-product-liability/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["AI programs ",["likely fit","https://scholarship.law.missouri.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2191&context=facpubs"]," the abnormally dangerous standard. The touchstone case was tried in the U.K. in 1868. In the decision, the ",["court stated","https://www.uni-trier.de/fileadmin/fb5/FFA/KURSUNTERLAGEN/Anglo-Amerikanisches_Recht/Law_of_Torts/Siry-SS-2012/Rylands_v_Fletcher__1868__UKHL_1__17_July_1868_.pdf"]," that if someone has “anything” under their power that is “likely to do mischief if it escapes, [he] must keep it in at his peril” and is “answerable for all the damage which is the natural consequence of its escape.” The defendant is liable even if they used “ ",["the utmost care to prevent the harm","https://opencasebook.org/casebooks/4643-tobia-torts-2022/resources/9.2.4-restatement-3d-liability-for-physical-and-emotional-harm-20-abnormally-dangerous-activities/"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["An attorney could pursue this avenue if a company builds AI software that is supposed to stay in a sandbox – a place isolated from the rest of a computer or network – but ",["loses control of it","https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/2026/09/ai-hacks-infestation/688806/"],". The AI industry’s recent admissions that the software creates all sorts of risks would make such cases stronger. When Anthropic filed for its initial public offering in October, numerous pages of the document ",["detailed extraordinary risks","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/anthropic-ipo-filing-ai-risks/"]," that its frontier AI models could pose."]},{"k":"p","s":["One hitch in applying this type of strict liability is that an activity must not be in ",["common usage","https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/abnormally_dangerous_activity"],". Lawyers could ",["make a strong case","https://scholarship.law.missouri.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2191&context=facpubs"]," against so-called ",["rogue AI","https://theconversation.com/the-wargames-problem-computer-science-has-long-understood-what-it-takes-to-keep-ai-under-control-292884"]," that runs wild and isn’t available to most people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Applying the danger standard could still fail to rein in AI companies or reward victims appropriately. In 1929, aviation was seen as ",["abnormally dangerous","https://opencasebook.org/casebooks/2566-torts/resources/19.4-crosby-v-cox-aircraft-co-the-airplane-that-ran-out-of-fuel/"],". But damages were capped at US$8,300, which was not a large deterrent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes changed in 1999, when the ",["Montreal Convention","https://www.congress.gov/treaty-document/106th-congress/45/document-text"]," standardized strict liability rules for international flights worldwide. It raised statutory damages and eliminated caps for negligence claims. Perhaps the most powerful tool in aviation liability today is for an authority to ground a company’s aircraft, which ",["happened to Boeing","https://www.cpajournal.com/2025/08/12/the-story-of-boeings-failed-corporate-culture-3/"]," after two fatal crashes with its 737 MAX planes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Guilty products"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Strict product liability","https://www.lexisnexis.com/community/insights/legal/b/thought-leadership/posts/understanding-the-interplay-between-strict-liability-and-products-liability"]," is the other strategy for holding AI companies responsible for harm. In years past, courts tended to not see software as a product because it is intangible. But ",["that view is shifting","https://humanoidliability.com/resources/ai-software-product-liability/#the-ruling-that-changed-everything"],". In recent lawsuits alleging that social media hurt people, courts did see social media as a product and concluded that ",["strict liability was applicable","https://www.mofo.com/resources/insights/250618-software-gains-new-status-as-a-product-under-strict-liability-law"],". Cases ",["against Facebook","https://theconversation.com/jury-finds-instagram-and-youtube-addictive-in-lawsuit-poised-to-reshape-social-media-platform-design-meets-product-liability-277066"]," have fallen into this category."]},{"k":"p","s":["Character.AI’s recent bankruptcy filing came in part because of a lawsuit in which the court ",["treated the software as a product","https://www.mofo.com/resources/insights/250618-software-gains-new-status-as-a-product-under-strict-liability-law"],". “ ",["Design defects","https://www.justia.com/products-liability/types-of-products-liability-claims/design-defects/"],"” is the part of the doctrine gaining traction. To use this, a plaintiff shows that the product posed a foreseeable risk to someone using it. So far, the doctrine has worked when applied to the lack of guardrails in chatbots."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pursuing strict liability could still run into snags. A court might order that AI software be turned off, or “grounded,” until it is improved. But as AI software creeps closer to being ",["an operating system","https://redmondmag.com/blogs/generationai/2026/07/building-an-ai-operating-system.aspx"]," and is evermore embedded in everyone’s daily activities, it becomes difficult to suspend its use."]},{"k":"h","s":["Moving target"]},{"k":"p","s":["AI software by its nature is constantly “learning” and therefore changing. It is impossible for a company to promise that AI software ",["will absolutely behave a certain way","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/products-liability-law-as-a-way-to-address-ai-harms/"],". In many cases, AI software is ",["inherently incapable","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=2959472"]," of supporting a guarantee about design safety. Still, strict liability is a way to hold the maker responsible, “even when those products ",["evolve in ways not specifically desired or foreseeable by their manufacturers","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/products-liability-law-as-a-way-to-address-ai-harms/"],",” according to a Brookings Institution report."]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe that if people are going to accept AI software as a boon to society, tough rules and sharp deterrents are needed. A strict liability system would shift risk from society to the companies seeking vast revenues."]},{"k":"p","s":["The next steps will be sorting out whether to treat all or some AI software as a product, and whether the technology is ultrahazardous. If it is treated as that dangerous, AI can develop with incentives to reduce harms and ensure that people injured are compensated."]}],"chars":5570},"https://theconversation.com/dna-study-of-ancient-cranes-suggests-we-need-to-rethink-how-many-species-have-gone-extinct-296569":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-19T00:28Z","sha":"04cc848b9e7d41689d1c70fb2974ad6c97f9f4bd101170cba6a12be1fa131d58","read":"https://theconversation.com/dna-study-of-ancient-cranes-suggests-we-need-to-rethink-how-many-species-have-gone-extinct-296569","bytes":189694,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"DNA study of ancient cranes suggests we need to rethink how many species have gone extinct","by":[{"n":"John Stewart","r":"Professor of Evolutionary Palaeoecology, Bournemouth University"},{"n":"Love Dalén","r":"Professor in Evolutionary Genomics, Stockholm University"},{"n":"Per Ericson","r":"Professor, Bioinformatics and Genetics, Swedish Museum of Natural History"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T14:53:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The human-driven extinction crisis that we are undoubtedly experiencing today is one of the great challenges of our age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Human-driven extinctions have been going on in some form for thousands of years. And birds have been ",["among the hardest hit","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41559-025-02746-z"],", with claims that they have experienced ",["higher levels of extinction","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-023-43445-2"]," than is often realised."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, it might be that some of these claimed extinctions require re-examination. ",["Our recent study","https://royalsocietypublishing.org/rsos/article/13/10/260699/483927/Ancient-DNA-study-resolves-the-taxonomic-status-of"]," used ancient DNA analyses to resolve the identity of a large crane known from remains dating from possibly 20,000 years ago or more, until about 1,000 years ago. This crane was classified 150 years ago as a distinct species known as Grus primigenia."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a longstanding controversy over whether the classification of this extinct continental bird is valid and reliable. This giant, primeval crane ",["was named","https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/141474#page/9/mode/1up"]," in the 19th century by the French biologist Alphonse Milne-Edwards, from bone fragments ",["found in caves","https://books.google.co.uk/books?hl=en&lr=&id=CBxjGyWC0iIC&oi=fnd&pg=PA473&ots=m9nSNEXEgI&sig=P_I97vZPocrAHBDKBTyLLLvWQL0&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q&f=false"]," in the south of France."]},{"k":"p","s":[["These first bones","https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Grus%20primigenia%E2%80%94europas%20utd%C3%B6da%20j%C3%A4ttetrana&author=T%20Tyrberg&publication_year=1985&journal=Fauna%20och%20Flora&volume=80&pages=169-176"]," attributed to Grus primigenia were dated to the end of the last ice age. Since then, ",["many other remains","https://www.barpublishing.com/book/an-evolutionary-study-of-some-archaeologically-significant-avian-taxa-in-the-quaternary-of-the-western-palaearctic/"]," of cranes have been attributed to the extinct species."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other ideas about the identity of these large cranes have been proposed over the years since their first description. Some authors suggested that they represented large living species ",["such as the sarus crane","https://bioone.org/journals/waterbirds/volume-41/issue-1/063.041.0111/The-Role-of-Artificial-Habitats-and-Rainfall-Patterns-in-the/10.1675/063.041.0111.short"]," Antigone antigone, found today in Asia and associated with monsoon climates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, some thought they might be ",["Siberian crane","https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/sibcra1/1.0/introduction"]," Leucogeranus leucogeranus, which breed in the tundra of eastern Siberia. However, the suggestion that they were simply ",["larger versions of the common crane","https://searchworks.stanford.edu/view/4404065"]," (Grus grus), still living in Europe today, has regularly been proposed."]},{"k":"p","s":["To investigate the identity of the primeval crane we sampled 18 crane bones from England, Wales, France, Germany and the Balearic Islands and included specimens of a variety of sizes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The results of the analysis, done at the Centre for Palaeogenetics in Stockholm, Sweden, strongly suggest that they all belonged to the same species, the living common crane, and that the other proposed identities could be excluded."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why so many species?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The next stage of the analysis was to determine why these large cranes had been given distinct species status. One of the justifications for their identification as a separate species was that there appeared to be two species in the past in Europe. The smaller individuals were thought to belong to the smaller common crane and larger ones were considered to be members of the extinct crane species."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, even before our findings were published, there was a clue that this was a misreading of the situation. A survey of the modern common crane revealed that male birds ",["exceed the size","https://www.barpublishing.com/book/an-evolutionary-study-of-some-archaeologically-significant-avian-taxa-in-the-quaternary-of-the-western-palaearctic/"]," of females; they are highly sexually “dimorphic” – where males and females of a species exhibit significant physical differences."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was important because when the ancient cranes were compared to the modern birds there appeared to be very few cranes in the past that were the size of modern female birds."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead, there were cranes that were the size of modern males and ones that were even larger. These larger birds have been attributed to the extinct species of crane. This appeared to suggest that the common crane had shrunk in size over time."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using a molecular genetic methodology, we uncovered the sexes of the crane specimens used in this study to determine if the larger birds were dominantly males and the ones that conformed to the size of modern males included females. The result was clear: size change and sexual dimorphism had erroneously implied that two separate species had lived in Europe during the last 20,000 years."]},{"k":"h","s":["Local extinction"]},{"k":"p","s":["The latest individuals that exceeded the modern common crane in size are from Lincolnshire in England. They had been excavated from an Anglo-Saxon archaeological site at Flixborough, where there was evidence that high-status people ",["may have feasted","https://www.oxbowbooks.com/9781842172902/farmers-monks-and-aristocrats/"]," on them."]},{"k":"p","s":["This indicates that some time during the approximately 1,000 years since the Lincolnshire finds, the common crane ",["shrank in size","https://www.britishbirds.co.uk/journal/article/wetland-birds-recent-fossil-record-britain-and-northwest-europe"],". Why this occurred is unclear, although the fact that the species disappeared from Britain and many parts of Europe since that time is probably relevant. However, the birds ",["returned to the UK","https://britishbirds.co.uk/journal/article/changing-status-common-crane-uk"]," of their own accord during the 1970s."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wetland drainage and hunting ",["have been blamed","https://britishbirds.co.uk/journal/article/changing-status-common-crane-uk"]," for the British local extinction about 400 years ago. The former is perhaps the most likely cause of the size decrease, as it might be symptomatic of habitat degradation across the birds’ range."]},{"k":"p","s":["The implications of this detailed analysis of the longest-standing controversy in recent avian extinction may be that caution ",["needs to be exercised","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/249334997_The_evidence_for_the_timing_of_speciation_of_modern_continental_birds_and_the_taxonomic_ambiguity_of_the_Quaternary_fossil_record"]," when reviews of historic extinctions are made."]},{"k":"p","s":["If birds are not identified from living individuals, like the great auk was, and are instead named based on the sizes of bones from the past, molecular analyses are probably needed to confirm that they are indeed separate species."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many extinct animals have been declared as species based on such characteristics. This suggests that at least some are likely to be differently sized individuals of the same species – not a separate one."]}],"chars":5171},"https://theconversation.com/ha-ti-lintervention-militaire-de-bukele-premier-test-a-letranger-de-sa-methode-contre-les-gangs-296691":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-19T16:34Z","sha":"4499858e21394d132546d69c99c10cf002f470b2bcb12815a3f46f0eb92f891f","read":"https://theconversation.com/ha-ti-lintervention-militaire-de-bukele-premier-test-a-letranger-de-sa-methode-contre-les-gangs-296691","bytes":198624,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Haïti : l’intervention militaire de Bukele, premier test à l’étranger de sa méthode contre les gangs","by":[{"n":"Robert Muggah","r":"Richard von Weizsäcker Fellow na Bosch Academy e Co-fundador, Instituto Igarapé; Princeton University"}],"pub":"2026-11-19T15:34:32Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["Le Salvador de Nayib Bukele déploie 2 500 soldats en Haïti pour combattre les gangs armés qui ont pris le contrôle de larges pans du pays."]},{"k":"li","s":["Les opérations militaires ont jusqu’ici été couronnées d’un certain succès, mais leurs effets sur la durée ne sont pas assurés et des inquiétudes sur les risques encourus par les populations civiles se font jour."]},{"k":"li","s":["L’intervention constitue un test grandeur nature de l’exportation du modèle sécuritaire de Bukele, déjà cité en exemple par de nombreux pays d’Amérique latine et au-delà."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le 10 novembre 2026, le président salvadorien Nayib Bukele a ",["diffusé des images","https://fr.africanews.com/amp/2026/11/11/haiti-les-militaires-salvadoriens-frappent-lun-des-principaux-gangs/"]," d’hélicoptères de combat ouvrant le feu sur un complexe situé près de Port-au-Prince, la capitale haïtienne."]},{"k":"p","s":["Quelques heures auparavant, il avait publié un message en créole haïtien sur les réseaux sociaux, demandant que lui soit communiquée l’adresse de Wilson Joseph, chef du gang 400 Mawozo, l’une des organisations criminelles les plus puissantes du pays. Bukele a ensuite affirmé que l’opération, menée conjointement avec la police haïtienne, avait permis de détruire la résidence de Joseph et le quartier général de son organisation. Jusqu’à 20 personnes auraient été tuées, même si le chef de gang était, selon les informations disponibles, absent au moment de l’attaque."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette offensive s’inscrit dans une multiplication des opérations contre les gangs en Haïti. Le 6 novembre, Mathias Saintil, chef du gang « Boston », implanté à Cité Soleil, a été ",["tué","https://www.guadeloupe.franceantilles.fr/actualite/faits-divers/haiti-le-chef-de-gang-mathias-saintil-est-mort-fusillade-ou-frappe-de-drone-1098979.php"]," lors d’une frappe de drone menée par une unité spéciale haïtienne. Le premier ministre Alix Didier Fils-Aimé avait alors ",["publié sur X","https://lenouvelliste.com/article/273679/le-premier-ministre-fils-aime-annonce-la-mort-de-mathias-saintil-lun-des-chefs-de-gangs-de-viv-ansanm"],": « Un chef de gang en moins. » Erik Prince, fondateur de la société militaire états-unienne privée Vectus Global, avait réagi par ces mots : « Bien joué. »"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Les sociétés militaires privées en Amérique latine : de la fin de la guerre froide à Vectus Global","https://theconversation.com/les-societes-militaires-privees-en-amerique-latine-de-la-fin-de-la-guerre-froide-a-vectus-global-291844"]]},{"k":"p","s":["En tant que ",["spécialiste du crime organisé en Amérique latine et dans les Caraïbes","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=oSuc5tUAAAAJ&hl=en"],", je considère que ces opérations marquent à la fois une escalade spectaculaire dans la lutte contre les organisations criminelles en Haïti et le premier test à l’étranger du modèle sécuritaire de Nayib Bukele. L’intervention suscite le ",["soutien de certains dirigeants de la région","https://apnews.com/article/dominican-republic-abinader-salvador-haiti-gangs-troops-55c1bdb8c82fce3b5d49ad33e6d8c194"]," et des réseaux favorables au président salvadorien. Mais les inquiétudes grandissent quant aux pertes civiles et à la capacité de cette opération militaire à déboucher sur une amélioration durable de la sécurité."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mission de sauvetage ou offensive militaire ?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Le Salvador était déjà présent, de manière limitée, en Haïti, parmi les ",["six pays fournissant des contingents à la Force de répression des gangs","https://press.un.org/en/2026/sc16482.doc.htm"]," (FRG) soutenue par les Nations unies. Autorisée en ",["2025","https://docs.un.org/en/S/RES/2793(2025)"],", cette force a pour mission d’aider les autorités haïtiennes à reprendre le contrôle des villes et des quartiers aux mains des gangs armés, qui dominent de vastes portions de ce pays particulièrement pauvre. Mais ses effectifs restent très inférieurs aux objectifs fixés, et elle peine à transformer ses opérations militaires en gains territoriaux durables."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le 18 octobre, quatre techniciens de l’aviation militaire salvadorienne, affectés à la FRG, ont disparu à la suite d’une embuscade tendue par des membres de gangs. ",["Leur véhicule incendié a été retrouvé","https://la1ere.franceinfo.fr/guadeloupe/en-haiti-le-vehicule-des-quatre-salvadoriens-disparus-retrouve-calcine-les-recherches-se-poursuivent-1755027.html"],", mais leur sort demeure incertain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Quoi qu’il en soit, Bukele s’est appuyé sur cet incident pour justifier un renforcement de la présence militaire salvadorienne en Haïti. En quelques semaines, il a envoyé environ 2 500 soldats, accompagnés de véhicules blindés et d’hélicoptères de combat. Il avait initialement présenté cette opération comme une mission de sauvetage destinée à retrouver ses compatriotes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces troupes sont venues s’ajouter à un dispositif sécuritaire déjà particulièrement complexe. La police et l’armée haïtiennes opèrent au côté de la FRG, autorisée par les Nations unies, mais qui ne relève pas directement de leur commandement. L’unité spéciale haïtienne impliquée dans les opérations contre Mathias Saintil travaille également avec Vectus Global, la société de sécurité fondée par l’ancien dirigeant de Blackwater, Erik Prince. Des groupes d’autodéfense patrouillent, quant à eux, dans les quartiers disputés."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dans le même temps, des dizaines de gangs armés, regroupés au sein de la ",["coalition Viv Ansanm (« Vivre ensemble »)","https://www.crisisgroup.org/fr/rpt/latin-america-caribbean/haiti/110-undoing-haitis-deadly-gang-alliance"],", contrôlent de larges portions de Port-au-Prince et opèrent également en dehors de la capitale."]},{"k":"p","s":["La Force de répression des gangs a été autorisée par le Conseil de sécurité de l’ONU à déployer jusqu’à 5 550 personnels. Elle ne compte actuellement qu’environ 2 000 hommes sur le terrain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Or, la majorité des soldats salvadoriens présents aujourd’hui en Haïti opèrent en dehors de son cadre de commandement. Le premier ministre haïtien, Alix Didier Fils-Aimé, affirme que les opérations restent placées sous l’autorité de son gouvernement. Pourtant, aucun des deux pays n’a rendu public l’accord définissant les prérogatives des forces salvadoriennes, leurs règles d’engagement ou la durée de leur déploiement."]},{"k":"p","s":["En l’absence d’un accord publié, la chaîne de commandement et les modalités d’autorisation des frappes restent donc opaques pour le public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Malgré le soutien apporté à Bukele par le président Donald Trump, le secrétaire d’État américain Marco Rubio a ",["pris ses distances avec l’offensive salvadorienne","https://rezonodwes.com/2026/11/haiti-salvador-rubio-veut-un-depart-rapide-des-salvadoriens-et-fils-aime/"],", affirmant que les États-Unis n’y participaient pas directement. Il a mis en garde contre les risques d’une mauvaise coordination, susceptible de provoquer des tirs amis. Les diplomates américains ont également exprimé officiellement leurs inquiétudes quant aux risques encourus par les troupes multinationales et le personnel civil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les autorités salvadoriennes ",["contestent","https://radioibo.ht/2026/11/10/le-salvador-conteste-les-problemes-de-coordination-signales-par-les-etats-unis/"]," les accusations américaines selon lesquelles leurs tirs auraient atteint l’ambassade des États-Unis et mis en danger les forces multinationales. Elles ont également ",["mis en cause","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/10/el-salvador-state-department-haiti-gangs"]," la crédibilité du principal représentant diplomatique américain en Haïti."]},{"k":"h","s":["Des règles d’engagement encore floues"]},{"k":"p","s":["La crise sécuritaire haïtienne a atteint un niveau alarmant."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces dernières années, les violences liées au crime organisé ont pris une ampleur comparable à celle observée dans des conflits armés. Près de ",["6 000 personnes","https://binuh.unmissions.org/en/binuh/communiques-de-presse/haiti-la-situation-des-droits-humains-reste-extremement-preoccupante-au"]," ont été tuées en 2025, et ",["plus de 4 000","https://efe.com/mundo/haiti-violencia-muertos-crisis-seguridad-tercer-trimestre-2026/"]," au cours des neuf premiers mois de 2026. En août 2026, près de 1,5 million d’Haïtiens avaient été ",["contraints de quitter leur domicile","https://dtm.iom.int/reports/haiti-report-internal-displacement-situation-round-14-august-2026"],". L’intensification des offensives militaires et les représailles des gangs pourraient provoquer de nouveaux déplacements de population."]},{"k":"p","s":["Une ",["analyse juridique indépendante","https://warwatch.ch/situations/non-international-armed-conflict-in-haiti/classification/"]," menée par l’Académie de droit international humanitaire et de droits humains de Genève qualifie les affrontements entre les forces haïtiennes et la coalition Viv Ansanm de « conflit armé non international », une catégorie juridique qui englobe notamment les guerres civiles. De son côté, le Comité international de la Croix-Rouge a ",["mis en garde","https://www.icrc.org/en/article/haiti-do-everything-possible-protect-population-effects-escalating-armed-violence"]," contre les risques encourus par les populations civiles, appelant toutes les parties à respecter le droit international."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette distinction est importante, car les règles encadrant le recours à la force létale diffèrent selon que l’on se trouve dans un contexte de guerre ou dans celui d’une opération de police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dans les deux cas, les civils doivent être protégés. Mais, dans un conflit armé, les membres de groupes armés qui participent directement aux combats peuvent être pris pour cible même lorsqu’ils ne représentent pas une menace immédiate. Dans le cadre d’une opération de police, en revanche, le simple fait d’être soupçonné d’appartenir à un gang ne suffit pas à justifier une mise à mort. Le recours à la force létale n’est généralement autorisé qu’en cas de nécessité pour protéger des vies humaines."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’utilisation croissante de drones explosifs et d’hélicoptères de combat dans des zones résidentielles est particulièrement préoccupante. Entre mars 2025 et janvier 2026, ",["au moins 1 243 personnes auraient été tuées lors de 141 opérations impliquant des drones","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/03/10/haiti-drone-strikes-put-residents-at-risk"],". Parmi elles, au moins 60 n’auraient eu aucun lien avec les gangs, dont 17 enfants. Ces opérations sont antérieures à l’escalade militaire salvadorienne, mais elles illustrent déjà les risques liés à l’utilisation d’armes explosives dans des zones densément peuplées."]},{"k":"p","s":["Par ailleurs, la superposition des mandats des forces étrangères et des sociétés militaires privées pourrait compliquer les enquêtes sur les pertes civiles et les éventuelles attaques illégales."]},{"k":"h","s":["L’exportation du modèle Bukele"]},{"k":"p","s":["Une partie de la population haïtienne, épuisée par l’insécurité, accueille favorablement cette intervention internationale."]},{"k":"p","s":["Des ",["rassemblements","https://efe.com/mundo/2026-11-07/marchas-apoyo-bukele-haiti/"]," ont été organisés en soutien aux soldats salvadoriens. Des manifestants ont brandi des bâtons et scandé le nom de Bukele. Une personnalité haïtienne de premier plan engagée dans la défense des droits humains a également ",["apporté son soutien au déploiement","https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/around-1000-soldiers-from-el-salvador-have-deployed-to-haiti-source-says-4976576"],", tout en rappelant que les habitants des quartiers contrôlés par les gangs ne sont pas nécessairement membres de ces organisations criminelles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukele fait activement la promotion de l’offensive en ",["diffusant des vidéos de soldats et de frappes aériennes","https://apnews.com/article/nayib-bukele-el-salvador-haiti-elections-war-on-gangs-un-rubio-democracy-5c8a5e284835778c31c9ff78c140afcd"],", relayées par les responsables salvadoriens et les influenceurs favorables à son gouvernement. Les messages en créole haïtien et en espagnol présentant les frappes comme des victoires contre les gangs rappellent la communication gouvernementale largement diffusée au Salvador, qui met en scène les arrestations massives et les transferts de détenus vers les prisons de haute sécurité."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depuis son arrivée au pouvoir en 2019, Bukele a ",["considérablement fait baisser le nombre d’homicides au Salvador","https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/10/21/salvador-derriere-la-chute-historique-de-la-criminalite-des-milliers-de-detenus-dans-l-attente-d-etre-juges_6798123_3210.html"],". Cette évolution a renforcé, ",["dans certaines parties de l’Amérique du Sud et des Caraïbes","https://www.project-syndicate.org/magazine/bukele-effect-in-latin-america-risks-to-replicating-el-salvador-model-by-robert-muggah-2026-03"],", l’idée qu’une politique de fermeté extrême face aux gangs peut justifier les atteintes aux droits humains qui l’accompagnent."]},{"k":"p","s":["En Amérique latine, ",["plusieurs responsables politiques","https://english.elpais.com/international/2023-03-17/bukele-intensifies-war-on-gangs-2000-more-inmates-transferred-to-biggest-prison-in-all-america.html"]," partisans d’une ligne sécuritaire dure se sont ainsi appuyés sur la baisse du taux d’homicides au Salvador pour promouvoir des politiques répressives similaires. Le président de la République dominicaine (seul pays ayant une frontière terrestre avec Haïti) ",["Luis Abinader","https://apnews.com/article/dominican-republic-abinader-salvador-haiti-gangs-troops-55c1bdb8c82fce3b5d49ad33e6d8c194"]," a, lui aussi, apporté son soutien à l’intervention, confirmant que son pays coopérait avec le Salvador en matière de logistique et de renseignement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pourtant, le modèle salvadorien repose largement sur le recours à l’état d’exception et sur l’incarcération massive. Environ ",["1,7 % de la population du Salvador serait aujourd’hui emprisonnée","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/10/07/el-salvador-mass-trials-a-mockery-of-justice"],", ce qui en ferait, de très loin, le ",["pays affichant le taux d’incarcération le plus élevé au monde","https://www.prisonstudies.org/world-prison-data/highest-lowest/highest-lowest-prison-population-rate?language_content_entity=en-gb"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["La situation haïtienne présente des difficultés opérationnelles bien plus importantes. Selon l’Office des Nations unies contre la drogue et le crime (ONUDC), les gangs contrôlent de vastes territoires, ",["disposent d’armes lourdes","https://www.unodc.org/unodc/frontpage/2024/April/haiti_-gangs-have-more-firepower-than-the-police.html"]," et entretiennent des liens avec des réseaux politiques et économiques. Les institutions haïtiennes sont beaucoup plus fragiles et les groupes armés ",["recrutent massivement des enfants dès leur plus jeune âge","https://childrenandarmedconflict.un.org/en/news/special-representative-secretary-general-children-and-armed-conflict-concludes-first-visit"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pour conserver les territoires reconquis, il faudrait donc pouvoir s’appuyer sur une police et une justice opérationnelles, mais aussi garantir la protection des habitants après le départ des forces étrangères."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le renforcement de la présence salvadorienne en Haïti comporte également des risques politiques pour les deux gouvernements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukele ",["cherchera à obtenir un troisième mandat lors de l’élection présidentielle de février 2027","https://www.france24.com/fr/am%C3%A9riques/20261001-elections-fixees-28-fevrier-salvador-nayib-bukele-briguer-troisieme-mandat-reelection-illimitee-guerre-gangs"],", après avoir fait passer une réforme constitutionnelle ayant supprimé la limitation du nombre de mandats présidentiels."]},{"k":"p","s":["La mort de militaires salvadoriens pourrait susciter des critiques dans son propre pays et le pousser à intensifier encore l’intervention, d’autant que les quatre techniciens dont la disparition a justifié la mission de sauvetage ",["n’ont toujours pas été retrouvés","https://www.latintimes.com/salvadoran-technicians-missing-haiti-gang-ambush-601077"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["En Haïti, Fils-Aimé a publiquement soutenu l’offensive à l’approche des ",["élections présidentielle et législatives prévues en juillet et octobre 2027","https://www.franceinfo.fr/replay-radio/d-un-monde-a-l-autre/haiti-sans-chef-de-l-etat-depuis-cinq-ans-organisera-des-elections-presidentielle-et-legislatives-en-2027_8241106.html"],". Des pertes civiles ou l’incapacité à conserver les territoires repris aux gangs pourraient fragiliser la crédibilité de son gouvernement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Au-delà des opérations militaires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ce déploiement pourrait préfigurer de nouveaux dispositifs régionaux de coopération en matière de sécurité."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le Salvador appartient au ",["Bouclier des Amériques","https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/03/06/le-bouclier-des-ameriques-confrerie-conservatrice-voulue-par-trump-en-amerique-latine-pour-contrer-la-chine_6669793_3210.html"]," (Shield of the Americas), une coalition soutenue par les États-Unis ",["lancée par Donald Trump en mars 2026","https://www.govinfo.gov/app/details/DCPD-202600155"]," afin de renforcer la coopération militaire contre les cartels de la drogue et les autres organisations criminelles transnationales."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’opération salvadorienne en Haïti ne relève pas officiellement de cette initiative, dont les ",["15 signataires","https://www.forth.news/lists/state/CfK5nG2Hm6uuvGtfSJ793"]," se sont engagés à renforcer leur coopération sécuritaire. Mais ce type de partenariat pourrait permettre à des gouvernements de la région de déployer des forces armées avec le soutien logistique des États-Unis, tout en limitant l’implication militaire directe de Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["Si l’intervention salvadorienne constitue le dernier exemple en date d’une opération de grande ampleur, j’ai pu observer des cycles similaires en Haïti depuis les années 2000."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entre 2007 et 2009, les Casques bleus de l’ONU et la police haïtienne avaient ",["repris le contrôle de plusieurs quartiers de Cité Soleil","https://news.un.org/fr/story/2007/03/105752"],", dans l’arrondissement de Port-au-Prince. Ces opérations avaient contribué à une réduction du nombre d’enlèvements, sans toutefois permettre de rétablir durablement la sécurité. Ensuite, après le séisme de 2010, la mission des Nations unies a involontairement été ",["à l’origine de l’introduction du choléra dans le pays","https://www.lemonde.fr/planete/article/2016/08/19/l-onu-admet-sa-responsabilite-dans-l-epidemie-de-cholera-en-haiti_4985249_3244.html"],". L’épidémie a provoqué la mort de plus de 9 000 personnes et conduit l’ONU à présenter des excuses officielles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Si les gangs survivent aux offensives militaires, c’est notamment parce que ",["leurs réseaux économiques restent opérationnels","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/opinion/article-haitis-elites-should-be-held-accountable-for-backing-gangs/"],". Ils tirent profit des enlèvements et des trafics illicites, tout en ",["contrôlant l’accès","https://www.americasquarterly.org/article/flows-of-guns-and-money-are-dooming-haiti/"]," à des axes routiers et à des marchés stratégiques. L’élimination de leurs chefs peut ",["affaiblir les organisations criminelles","https://my.rusi.org/resource/criminal-governance-politics-of-control-in-latin-america-and-the-caribbean.html"],", mais elle ne suffit pas à tarir les sources de financement qui leur permettent de fonctionner."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’offensive salvadorienne pourrait donc produire des résultats sécuritaires à court terme. Mais leur pérennité dépendra de la capacité des institutions haïtiennes à conserver le contrôle des territoires reconquis."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’intervention de Bukele constitue désormais un test à l’étranger d’un modèle sécuritaire qui bénéficie d’un attrait politique considérable. Mais ses véritables résultats ne pourront être évalués qu’à une seule aune : les Haïtiens seront-ils plus en sécurité lorsque les forces étrangères auront quitté le pays ?"]}],"chars":14588},"https://theconversation.com/who-is-jess-wilson-victorias-new-premier-296287":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-28T10:09Z","sha":"dd89cf47aed9231256ccd758cd97485a5a29ab699f019836e25909217c19aad2","read":"https://theconversation.com/who-is-jess-wilson-victorias-new-premier-296287","bytes":178801,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Who is Jess Wilson, Victoria’s new premier?","by":[{"n":"Finley Watson","r":"PhD Candidate, Politics, La Trobe University"},{"n":"Phoebe Hayman","r":"PhD Candidate and Casual Academic in Politics, La Trobe University"}],"pub":"2026-11-28T08:53:59Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In a confirmation of ",["recent polls","https://www.roymorgan.com/findings/10398-victorian-state-voting-intention-webinar-november-2026"],", Opposition Leader Jess Wilson has become Victoria’s new premier."]},{"k":"p","s":["At 36, the former Young Liberal president, first-term member and first female state Liberal leader has become the youngest premier since Federation. Wilson argues her youth offers “ ",["fresh ideas and energy","https://www.thedailyaus.com.au/videos/who-is-jess-wilson-interview-with-victoria-opposition-leader"],"” for the state. It may also prove her greatest challenge."]},{"k":"h","s":["Blue blood"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although she is only just beginning her second term in parliament, Wilson’s life has been deeply enmeshed in the Liberal Party. The daughter of a former Victorian Liberal MP Ron Wilson, Jess joined the Young Liberals while at university, ",["serving as president","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/victoria/ex-frydenberg-staffer-shapes-as-front-runner-to-take-smith-s-kew-seat-20211107-p596p2.html"]," in 2016."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of her ",["personal and professional relationships","https://www.afr.com/politics/jess-wilson-s-network-is-full-of-ceos-millennials-and-ipa-grads-20261111-p61cwa"]," stem from this period, and Wilson is now married to another Young Liberals ",["president","https://www.crikey.com.au/2026/11/18/jess-wilson-debate-millennials-victorian-state-election/"],", former Institute of Public Affairs (IPA) research fellow Aaron Lane."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson has worked as an adviser to former federal deputy leader Josh Frydenberg and is close friends with Victorian senator ",["James Paterson","https://www.smh.com.au/national/victoria/this-daggy-millennial-has-always-wanted-to-be-in-charge-she-even-arrested-her-sister-20261113-p61dhi.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prior to her election as the member for Kew at the 2022 state election, Wilson had a stint as a consultant at KPMG, before working on policy at the ",["Business Council of Australia","https://www.victorianchamber.com.au/profile/jess-wilson-mp"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson says this role, and her experience working on government-business relations during the COVID pandemic, shaped her decision to ",["enter parliament","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/ng-interactive/2026/oct/31/who-is-jess-wilson-mp-victoria-election-2026-liberal-leader-profile-interview-ntwnfb"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A fresh start for the Liberal Party?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson’s policy priorities have changed significantly in the past four years."]},{"k":"p","s":["During her 2022 campaign she advocated a transition to a renewable, net-zero economy without gas. A year later she became the only Victorian Liberal to support the Voice to Parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, in 2026 she has promised to introduce legislation to ",["abolish","https://www.jesswilsonkew.com.au/news/2026-10-17-lowering-energy-and-housing-costs-by-scrapping-labors-gas-ban"]," Victoria’s gas ban and ",["repeal","https://www.jesswilsonkew.com.au/news/2026-05-01-repealing-treaty-to-save-taxpayers-1-billion"]," its First Peoples Treaty. She has also, controversially, ",["announced","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/27/one-nation-wont-support-coalition-plan-to-privatise-melbournes-sewage-plants-price-rises-poor-services"]," she will raise money by selling off Melbourne’s sewage treatment plants for 90 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["These changes have raised ",["questions from journalists","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-g-OXxgREg8"]," on the campaign trail, who have attempted to pin down Wilson’s priorities. Her responses have appeared only to create further confusion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Questions have also come from the political right. During the leaders’ debate, One Nation Leader Warren Pickering asked Wilson if the Coalition remained committed to ",["net zero by 2035","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-18/victorian-election-debate-jess-wilson-winner/107397070"],". Wilson avoided explicit commitments, saying her only focus was on “ ",["reliable and affordable power","https://www.facebook.com/OneNationVictoria/posts/last-night-liberal-leader-jess-wilson-was-asked-about-her-commitment-to-net-zero/1654492156460883/"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was part of a broader line of attack, in which One Nation mocked the Liberal Party’s commitments to a “Fresh Start for Victoria”. One Nation campaign materials accused Labor and Liberals of being identical, using the tagline “ ",["There’s nothing fresh about the same old thing","https://www.facebook.com/reel/1154653656980812"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson’s policy centrepiece, “ ",["Our First 100 Days","https://www.jesswilsonkew.com.au/news/2026-08-19-liberals-and-nationals-launch-our-first-100-days-plan"],"” was used by the Liberal campaign to define the new premier as proactive and responsive, in contrast to the ageing Labor government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whether the new government can fulfil these promises while reducing Victoria’s debt has been questioned during the campaign. The responsibility for this lands squarely on Wilson herself, who ",["has stated","https://www.afr.com/politics/federal/what-a-wilson-cabinet-could-look-like-but-does-she-have-the-depth-20261120-p61ere"]," she will serve as both premier and treasurer for the first three months."]},{"k":"p","s":["To pull it off, Wilson will need to hit the ground running and keep the Liberal party room united."]},{"k":"h","s":["Uniting a broad, and often fractious, church"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson’s political beliefs have been criticised for their ",["ambiguity","https://www.3aw.com.au/jacqui-felgate-turns-up-the-heat-on-jess-wilson-about-nuclear-power/"],". Her statements, associations and policies offers clues, but not answers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although she has often been associated with the Liberal Party’s moderate faction, Wilson has resisted this description, preferring to refer to herself as a “ ",["classical, small-l liberal","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-11-19/victoria-liberal-party-gamble-jess-wilson-survival-federal/106024478"],"” and someone who cares more about the economy than culture wars when asked about her political alignment."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, her connections to the IPA have put her at odds with moderates in the past. As president of the Young Liberals, Wilson withstood a ",["challenge","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2016-06-30/turf-wars-young-liberals/7553020"]," from a group who were concerned with the conservative think tank’s influence over the Liberal Party."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ambiguity of Wilson’s political loyalties may have assisted her rise in parliament. She was first promoted as a unifying force in the party in 2024 as a potential deputy in Brad Battin’s leadership challenge against John Pesutto. She was seen as a presence capable of representing both moderates and conservatives and of being ",["the face of a more modern Liberal Party","https://web.archive.org/web/20241223072327/https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/dec/23/victorian-liberal-party-leadership-spill-john-pesutto-brad-battin-ntwnfb"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As leader, Wilson appears to have succeeded in unifying personalities and policies in the lead up to the election. Now in government and likely to face much closer scrutiny, Wilson will need to engage with the questions of her own party that she has so far managed to avoid."]},{"k":"p","s":["If she can answer these, she’ll be the leader of a more modern Victorian Liberal Party. If not, Victoria’s “fresh start” may soon grow stale."]}],"chars":4677}};
